WEBVTT


00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.300
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:45.902 --> 00:00:47.907
[crowd chanting]
Pink Slip! Pink Slip!


00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:50.415
Pink Slip! Pink Slip!


00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.909
Pink Slip! Pink Slip!


00:00:52.044 --> 00:00:53.984
[guitar playing]


00:01:09.997 --> 00:01:11.392
[phone chimes]


00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:12.994
[Siri] <i>Text from Mom:</i>


00:01:13.129 --> 00:01:14.822
<i>"Hi, honey. I noticed
you haven't chimed in</i>


00:01:14.905 --> 00:01:16.337
<i>on the family chat."</i>


00:01:16.472 --> 00:01:18.120
<i>Text from Mom: "Maybe
we can all FaceTime?"</i>


00:01:18.203 --> 00:01:19.603
<i>Text from Mom:</i>


00:01:19.739 --> 00:01:20.895
<i>"I'm just about to
record a new episode."</i>


00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:22.006
[♪ "Rebel Rebel" playing]


00:01:22.141 --> 00:01:23.514
Hi. Welcome back.


00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.180
I'm Dr. Tess Coleman,


00:01:25.316 --> 00:01:27.947
and this is <i>Rebelling
with Respect</i>.


00:01:28.082 --> 00:01:29.811
Today on the podcast,


00:01:29.946 --> 00:01:32.383
we are talking about
a relationship dynamic


00:01:32.518 --> 00:01:34.789
that is very close to my heart.


00:01:34.924 --> 00:01:37.160
"Grand co-parenting."


00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:40.257
When my daughter, Anna,
chose to become a single mom,


00:01:40.393 --> 00:01:41.993
it changed our family forever.


00:01:42.129 --> 00:01:43.798
[mechanical buzzing]


00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.230
Ryan! Cloffice. Recording.


00:01:46.365 --> 00:01:48.129
[Ryan clears throat, spits]


00:01:48.264 --> 00:01:49.906
Sorry!


00:01:50.375 --> 00:01:54.741
As a grandma, I was able
to step up and help her.


00:01:54.876 --> 00:01:56.343
[alarm ringing]


00:01:58.808 --> 00:02:01.583
[Anna] Harper! [breathes deeply]


00:02:02.252 --> 00:02:04.149
Harper, this is your
30-minute warning


00:02:04.285 --> 00:02:06.188
that we're leaving for school.


00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.392
Harp?


00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.786
This is now your
20-minute warning.


00:02:11.387 --> 00:02:12.390
Ten minutes.


00:02:12.526 --> 00:02:14.298
Yes, confirm the
recording sessions.


00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.000
But know that I know she can
sell out more than the Greek.


00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.765
And yes, I know how
many seats there are.


00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.335
[knocks on door]


00:02:20.471 --> 00:02:22.016
[Anna] Harper! I really
wanna respect your space,


00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:24.102
but I'm curious as to why
you're not out here yet.


00:02:24.237 --> 00:02:25.738
You have five minutes!


00:02:25.873 --> 00:02:28.210
[Tess] <i>Being someone that
your loved one can lean on</i>


00:02:28.346 --> 00:02:31.774
is the most important
relationship there is.


00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.950
Ryan, I'm getting
so good at this!


00:02:38.085 --> 00:02:40.189
[computer chimes]


00:02:40.591 --> 00:02:41.960
No.


00:02:43.419 --> 00:02:44.485
No, no, no!


00:02:44.921 --> 00:02:47.059
-Oh, it didn't record!
-[beeping]


00:02:47.194 --> 00:02:48.798
-Moth...
-[beeping]


00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.065
-[phone ringing]
-Hi, Mom.


00:02:50.201 --> 00:02:51.697
Now is not a great
time. I'm just...


00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:53.352
[Tess] <i>I know, but I
finished my podcast early,</i>


00:02:53.435 --> 00:02:55.205
<i>so I'm offering to do drop-off.</i>


00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.905
No. It's okay. I've got
everything under control.


00:02:58.308 --> 00:03:00.005
Harper, you had to be
up ten minutes ago!


00:03:00.141 --> 00:03:01.469
Prepare to be triggered!


00:03:01.605 --> 00:03:02.904
[♪ "HOT TO GO!" playing]


00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.185
Harper!


00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:23.428
-Let's catch one more.
-[surfers chuckling]


00:03:23.563 --> 00:03:25.530
[surfer] Dude, these
waves are unreal.


00:03:25.666 --> 00:03:28.004
[Harper] I love our
lives! [chuckling]


00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.936
Yo, are we skipping
first period?


00:03:30.072 --> 00:03:31.900
Oh, shoot. We gotta go.


00:03:39.951 --> 00:03:41.217
-Harper!
-[Harper] What?


00:03:41.886 --> 00:03:42.981
I'm literally ready.


00:03:43.116 --> 00:03:44.755
Barely. Barely.


00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.615
I made your favorite lunch.


00:03:47.117 --> 00:03:49.256
How was pickleball
yesterday? Did you beat 'em?


00:03:49.392 --> 00:03:52.292
-We say "annihilated."
-[chuckling]


00:03:52.427 --> 00:03:54.488
Mom, I told you
I could take her.


00:03:54.624 --> 00:03:55.556
I know, sweetheart.


00:03:55.692 --> 00:03:57.024
But I saw on your stories


00:03:57.159 --> 00:03:58.835
that you were working
at the studio late,


00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:00.468
and so I decided to take her.


00:04:00.604 --> 00:04:02.655
You know, it would be healthy
for you to unfollow me.


00:04:02.738 --> 00:04:04.973
And I work late all the
time. I can still take her.


00:04:05.109 --> 00:04:07.440
Anna, let's pause and reframe.


00:04:07.575 --> 00:04:09.477
When you decided
to be a single mom,


00:04:09.612 --> 00:04:11.578
I told you I would support
you a hundred percent.


00:04:11.713 --> 00:04:14.442
Well, this is me supporting
you a hundred percent.


00:04:14.578 --> 00:04:15.882
Okay, you know what?


00:04:16.017 --> 00:04:17.251
I'm coming too.


00:04:17.387 --> 00:04:18.827
We can both do
drop-off this morning.


00:04:18.916 --> 00:04:21.049
-[Anna] Mom.
-No, go on. You can go.


00:04:21.184 --> 00:04:22.875
-[Anna] Just let them...
-Oh, okay, you're not going.


00:04:22.958 --> 00:04:24.027
[horns honking]


00:04:24.162 --> 00:04:25.322
-[Anna] Mom.
-You're gonna go.


00:04:25.428 --> 00:04:26.682
You're not... Nobody's gonna go.


00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:27.993
I'm gonna go!


00:04:28.696 --> 00:04:30.993
-So what's up, kiddo?
-[Harper] Nothing.


00:04:31.696 --> 00:04:33.071
-Okay, spill it.
-All right.


00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:35.338
My new lab partner is
the absolute worst.


00:04:35.473 --> 00:04:37.465
<i>She's the new girl,
here for the year.</i>


00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.834
<i>I mean, ugh,</i>


00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.308
<i>she thinks she's so much better</i>


00:04:40.443 --> 00:04:42.444
<i>than everyone because
she's British,</i>


00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.347
which she has to remind
you of every five seconds.


00:04:45.482 --> 00:04:47.451
Like no one's ever been
from England before.


00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.832
[lab partner] So my dad opened
his third restaurant in Paris,


00:04:49.915 --> 00:04:51.621
and that's how I met
my French boyfriend,


00:04:51.756 --> 00:04:52.880
Philippe Henri.


00:04:53.016 --> 00:04:55.483
-[sighs] Philippe Henri.
-Ooh, la-la.


00:04:55.619 --> 00:04:56.952
He's French and a model.


00:04:57.088 --> 00:04:58.895
You've seriously been
to Paris Fashion Week?


00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.228
Anna Wintour scowled at me.


00:05:00.364 --> 00:05:02.164
-Seriously?
-What's Paris like?


00:05:02.299 --> 00:05:04.393
Oh, it's lovely.
I go all the time.


00:05:04.529 --> 00:05:06.127
Ignore the British girl.


00:05:06.262 --> 00:05:09.004
After this year, you won't
have to see her anymore.


00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.900
Nice advice from a therapist.


00:05:11.035 --> 00:05:12.969
Well, I'm not her
therapist. I'm her Gram.


00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:14.395
[Harper] All right,
well, this has been real.


00:05:14.478 --> 00:05:16.345
Please drive away like
you don't know me.


00:05:17.046 --> 00:05:18.114
Make good choices!


00:05:18.249 --> 00:05:20.242
-You are so lame.
-[horn honking]


00:05:20.377 --> 00:05:21.449
Lame!


00:05:21.851 --> 00:05:24.005
[in British accent] Are you
ready for laboratory today?


00:05:24.088 --> 00:05:25.413
Shut your mouth. [chuckles]


00:05:25.549 --> 00:05:26.617
[bell ringing]


00:05:26.753 --> 00:05:28.682
[teacher] Fun bonus round today.


00:05:28.818 --> 00:05:31.129
Never trust an atom. Why?


00:05:33.024 --> 00:05:35.024
'Cause they make up
everything. [chuckles]


00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.793
Here all day, folks.


00:05:36.929 --> 00:05:38.346
You're supposed to
put your goggles on


00:05:38.429 --> 00:05:39.632
before we start.


00:05:40.402 --> 00:05:42.071
The goggles are giving Minion.


00:05:42.206 --> 00:05:44.038
Yeah. We're not, like, Minions.


00:05:44.641 --> 00:05:47.543
So, no, thank you. But
they're perfect for you.


00:05:48.313 --> 00:05:50.207
It's like the Revolutionary War


00:05:50.342 --> 00:05:51.342
was for nothing.


00:05:51.614 --> 00:05:55.351
Today, remember, these
are dangerous chemicals.


00:05:55.486 --> 00:05:57.131
Maybe we should use
not-dangerous chemicals?


00:05:57.214 --> 00:05:58.841
How about you do your
actual share of the work


00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.124
instead of doodling?


00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:01.659
[lab partner] It's
called designing.


00:06:01.953 --> 00:06:03.624
The measurements
have to be precise.


00:06:04.327 --> 00:06:05.889
This experiment is so simple.


00:06:06.024 --> 00:06:08.223
In the UK, we did this
in primary school.


00:06:09.093 --> 00:06:10.827
The only reason people
think you're smart


00:06:10.962 --> 00:06:13.070
is because of your
obnoxious accent.


00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:15.664
At least people
think I'm clever.


00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.105
What's that supposed to mean?


00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.210
You're smart. Figure it out.


00:06:21.407 --> 00:06:22.471
-Oh, no.
-Oh, no.


00:06:22.606 --> 00:06:23.672
-Oh, no.
-Oh, no.


00:06:23.808 --> 00:06:25.183
[Harper, lab partner] Oh, no.


00:06:25.783 --> 00:06:26.783
Oh!


00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:30.782
-That was not precise!
-That's not precise at all!


00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.948
Oh. Principal Waldman!


00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:35.409
I don't know, Mom.
I don't know why


00:06:35.492 --> 00:06:36.972
the principal called
me, but I'm here.


00:06:37.088 --> 00:06:38.512
So you don't need to
come. You know what?


00:06:38.595 --> 00:06:39.940
I can't find what I was
gonna tell you about.


00:06:40.023 --> 00:06:41.823
-I'll call you...
-[grunts]


00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:43.367
-Sorry.
-It's totally my fault.


00:06:43.502 --> 00:06:45.799
No, no, no. I-I wasn't
looking where I was going.


00:06:45.935 --> 00:06:47.062
Oh.


00:06:53.771 --> 00:06:55.404
-Are you okay?
-[sighs]


00:06:55.539 --> 00:06:56.740
[phone ringing]


00:06:56.876 --> 00:06:58.382
-[stammers] Your phone.
-Yeah, I...


00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:00.879
Yeah, I don't know how
to turn this thing off.


00:07:01.014 --> 00:07:02.779
Yeah, I'm not sure,
either. I think, maybe...


00:07:02.915 --> 00:07:04.155
-I think you got it.
-Is it off?


00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.715
-Yeah. It's just...
-Oh, thank you.


00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.315
-No problem.
-Thank you.


00:07:07.451 --> 00:07:08.451
[sighs]


00:07:08.557 --> 00:07:10.895
Um, my daughter
just started here,


00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.430
and I admit I'm quite lost.


00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:14.416
Would you happen to know
where the chemistry lab is?


00:07:14.499 --> 00:07:17.158
This is serious. Someone
could have been injured.


00:07:17.293 --> 00:07:19.013
I'm sure it was just
an accident. [chuckles]


00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:21.739
It seems to me a
misunderstanding.


00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:24.572
Harper seems so...


00:07:25.502 --> 00:07:26.574
lovely.


00:07:26.709 --> 00:07:30.681
Oh. Well, Lily seems
so genuine and kind.


00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.348
[both chuckling]


00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:35.449
Wow. I certainly
never had two parents


00:07:35.585 --> 00:07:37.414
come in here and
be this attractive.


00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.149
I meant "attentive."


00:07:39.285 --> 00:07:40.457
Oh.


00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:42.925
Uh, Lily and I are
definitely going to reflect


00:07:43.061 --> 00:07:44.956
on how to do better.


00:07:45.092 --> 00:07:48.559
This is all Harper and I
are going to think about.


00:07:48.694 --> 00:07:51.225
We're very, very committed.


00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:55.563
Especially as a
single-parent household.


00:07:55.698 --> 00:07:56.832
Oh, us too.


00:07:56.967 --> 00:07:58.368
-We're single. Parent.
-Great.


00:07:58.504 --> 00:07:59.504
I mean, uh...


00:07:59.875 --> 00:08:02.303
-I'm a single parent, yeah.
-Single parent. Great.


00:08:02.438 --> 00:08:04.381
-Yeah. You know what I mean.
-Yes. Same. Me too.


00:08:04.948 --> 00:08:05.949
Single.


00:08:06.084 --> 00:08:07.541
Single parent. Guilty.


00:08:07.676 --> 00:08:08.609
Great.


00:08:08.744 --> 00:08:09.945
I'm single too.


00:08:10.081 --> 00:08:11.555
Oh, my God... Should we meet up?


00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.952
Perhaps our daughters should
get to know each other?


00:08:14.088 --> 00:08:16.620
Maybe, like, Wednesdays,
after 6:00. Get a little wine?


00:08:16.756 --> 00:08:18.490
Talk about these badass kids?


00:08:18.626 --> 00:08:20.225
Harper would really like that.


00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.492
Over dinner?


00:08:21.627 --> 00:08:22.866
Dinner sounds perfect.


00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:24.227
[Waldman] I'm on it.


00:08:25.331 --> 00:08:28.796
<i>Petit Trois</i>? Yes, can
I have a table for two?


00:08:28.931 --> 00:08:31.174
Private. In the back.


00:08:31.309 --> 00:08:32.810
Do you guys have any allergies?


00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:34.009
-No.
-No.


00:08:34.144 --> 00:08:35.210
No. No allergies.


00:08:35.346 --> 00:08:37.975
[♪ "Heart Attack" playing]


00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:27.460
[Tess] Okay, you came
here early. Spill it.


00:09:27.595 --> 00:09:28.860
[Anna] There's just no time.


00:09:28.995 --> 00:09:30.761
Bachelorette party,
dance rehearsal,


00:09:30.896 --> 00:09:32.628
final fitting, rehearsal lunch.


00:09:32.764 --> 00:09:34.231
And, oh, my wedding.


00:09:34.366 --> 00:09:37.340
You have a lot on your
plate. Big day. Deep breath.


00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.067
There's so much to
do before Sunday.


00:09:39.203 --> 00:09:40.644
Anna, let us know
how we can help.


00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.288
Maybe someone could help me
memorize my wedding vows.


00:09:42.371 --> 00:09:43.858
[Harper] How about
this? I'll help you.


00:09:43.941 --> 00:09:45.647
"I, Anna, take you, Eric,


00:09:45.782 --> 00:09:48.647
a man that I have been
dating for six months,


00:09:48.782 --> 00:09:50.613
but might uproot my entire life


00:09:50.749 --> 00:09:52.182
and move to London,


00:09:52.317 --> 00:09:55.359
"where we have no family
and an avocado costs $11."


00:09:55.495 --> 00:09:57.318
Perhaps you should
add something about


00:09:57.453 --> 00:10:00.459
my undying patience
for teenage rebellion.


00:10:00.595 --> 00:10:01.612
Spot on about the avocado.


00:10:01.695 --> 00:10:03.161
Oh. That wasn't about you.


00:10:03.296 --> 00:10:05.760
It was actually about my
mom's other British fiancé.


00:10:05.896 --> 00:10:07.062
She's a comedian today.


00:10:07.198 --> 00:10:08.486
-Just today, though.
-I see. Yeah.


00:10:08.569 --> 00:10:09.735
[Anna] Right, Harper?


00:10:09.871 --> 00:10:11.087
I have been practicing
our first dance.


00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.650
Wait till you see
what I have cooking.


00:10:12.773 --> 00:10:14.804
Ooh, I see what you did there.


00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.739
I missed you since yesterday.


00:10:16.875 --> 00:10:18.474
-Ew.
-[chuckles]


00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.178
[radio host] <i>Trevor Travis
just dropped a new single.</i>


00:10:21.314 --> 00:10:23.316
<i>I think we can all guess
who it might be about.</i>


00:10:23.452 --> 00:10:24.612
[music playing on radio]


00:10:24.747 --> 00:10:25.985
Hello?


00:10:26.421 --> 00:10:27.757
[horn blares]


00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:30.851
I had my pastry chef make
sticky toffee pudding pavlova


00:10:30.986 --> 00:10:32.188
for the bake sale.


00:10:32.323 --> 00:10:34.697
Just what every
teenager loves. Pavlova.


00:10:34.832 --> 00:10:37.425
Agreed. Teenagers these
days, sophisticated palates.


00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:41.538
Yes, well, this pastry
chef was up at 4:00 a.m.


00:10:41.673 --> 00:10:43.668
baking old-fashioned
chocolate chip cookies


00:10:43.803 --> 00:10:45.503
from scratch, with no staff.


00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:48.004
Four hours for cookies?


00:10:48.139 --> 00:10:50.041
I think we need to
get you a staff.


00:10:51.712 --> 00:10:53.174
They just needed to cool.


00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:54.815
Stand up straight. Good posture.


00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:56.435
Okay. And do you know
how bad this is for you?


00:10:56.518 --> 00:10:58.318
Seriously, eat this.


00:10:58.454 --> 00:11:00.353
Say, "Thanks, Mom."


00:11:00.489 --> 00:11:01.419
I saw that, Harper.


00:11:01.555 --> 00:11:02.486
[horn honking]


00:11:02.621 --> 00:11:04.055
Any day now.


00:11:05.158 --> 00:11:06.823
Just trying to keep
us on a schedule here.


00:11:06.959 --> 00:11:08.190
[in British accent] Oi. Well,


00:11:08.326 --> 00:11:10.527
we wouldn't want to be
off schedule, innit?


00:11:10.662 --> 00:11:11.662
Step, and...


00:11:11.761 --> 00:11:12.827
Hi, Lil!


00:11:12.962 --> 00:11:13.962
[Lily] It's Lily.


00:11:14.072 --> 00:11:15.598
Lily, back seat.


00:11:16.234 --> 00:11:17.627
[normal voice] Can't
Grams just take me?


00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.635
No, this will be good
bonding for everyone.


00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.038
Well, I bond best with Lily


00:11:22.174 --> 00:11:23.390
when we're not
around each other,


00:11:23.473 --> 00:11:25.305
and I don't have to
look at her face.


00:11:25.441 --> 00:11:27.217
Yeah, I love
sitting next to you.


00:11:27.352 --> 00:11:28.811
Reminds me that I'm amazing.


00:11:28.947 --> 00:11:30.246
[Tess] Seat belts, girls.


00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.557
-[horn honks]
-[both laughing]


00:11:37.692 --> 00:11:38.988
[Ryan] All right. All right.


00:11:39.123 --> 00:11:40.287
-I got you.
-You got me.


00:11:40.422 --> 00:11:42.061
-Good morning.
-We're ready to go.


00:11:42.197 --> 00:11:44.697
Good morning. Car's all
set. Up the coast, Route 1?


00:11:44.833 --> 00:11:47.266
-Yeah?
-Yeah? What do you think?


00:11:47.401 --> 00:11:50.374
[Tess] I'm not saying I don't
not want to go on the trip.


00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:53.774
I'm just saying
that Anna's wedding


00:11:53.909 --> 00:11:55.642
has put me behind
with my patients,


00:11:55.777 --> 00:11:57.710
which has been very disruptive.


00:11:57.846 --> 00:12:00.348
-Uh-huh.
-And... And, of course,


00:12:00.817 --> 00:12:03.454
they keep adding
dates to my book tour,


00:12:03.589 --> 00:12:05.849
which, you know, it's
out of my control.


00:12:06.318 --> 00:12:07.918
And I'm just saying
I need a little time.


00:12:08.051 --> 00:12:09.385
Look, girls. [sighs]


00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:11.861
We're trying to hear you.
Just try and hear us?


00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:13.089
Oh, no.


00:12:13.224 --> 00:12:14.594
I hear you trying
to pull me away


00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.130
from my family and my friends.


00:12:17.266 --> 00:12:19.832
I mean, who even gets to
surf before school in London?


00:12:19.968 --> 00:12:22.267
You can surf on
the river Thames.


00:12:22.403 --> 00:12:23.700
Really?


00:12:23.835 --> 00:12:24.966
No, you dipstick.


00:12:25.102 --> 00:12:26.300
-Girls.
-It's a city.


00:12:26.436 --> 00:12:27.756
-You need to...
-Okay, girls. Girls.


00:12:27.839 --> 00:12:28.940
It's our decision.


00:12:29.342 --> 00:12:31.546
Eric and I will do what's
right for the family.


00:12:31.681 --> 00:12:32.907
-Hmm.
-[Harper] Family?


00:12:33.042 --> 00:12:34.176
Yes, this family.


00:12:34.312 --> 00:12:35.816
-Don't say it like that.
-Don't say...


00:12:35.952 --> 00:12:37.133
-That sounds really cringe.
-Don't tell me


00:12:37.216 --> 00:12:38.598
-what to say and how to say.
-[sighs]


00:12:38.681 --> 00:12:39.965
[Lily] Harper, relax.
Don't be so dramatic.


00:12:40.048 --> 00:12:41.083
[Eric] Lily.


00:12:41.218 --> 00:12:42.922
-Stop gaslighting.
-What?


00:12:43.057 --> 00:12:45.256
You don't even know
what that means.


00:12:45.391 --> 00:12:46.713
[Harper] I don't wanna
look at your face anymore.


00:12:46.796 --> 00:12:48.393
You know what that means, right?


00:12:48.529 --> 00:12:49.849
-I think I know what it means.
-[Anna] Yeah. I knew you did.


00:12:49.932 --> 00:12:51.561
That explains why
you talk rubbish.


00:12:51.697 --> 00:12:54.762
[Waldman] <i>For the bake sale,
every table must have...</i>


00:12:54.897 --> 00:12:56.333
Okay.


00:12:56.469 --> 00:12:57.622
<i>...a gluten-free option,
an egg-free option...</i>


00:12:57.705 --> 00:12:59.368
Please don't slam the...


00:13:00.804 --> 00:13:01.902
door.


00:13:02.572 --> 00:13:04.405
Well, at least we don't
have to bring them


00:13:04.541 --> 00:13:06.512
to our immigration
interview tomorrow.


00:13:07.115 --> 00:13:09.613
Don't be stressed.
They'll come round.


00:13:10.382 --> 00:13:12.887
Yeah, let them take
all the time they need.


00:13:14.324 --> 00:13:16.790
[artist singing]


00:13:16.926 --> 00:13:18.523
He sounds great. I'll
be back in a bit.


00:13:19.159 --> 00:13:20.956
-Here's Ella's schedule.
-Thank you.


00:13:21.558 --> 00:13:23.180
Oh, send those to the
tour manager, please.


00:13:23.263 --> 00:13:25.326
-Yeah, okay.
-[singer] Okay? Because I'm...


00:13:25.462 --> 00:13:27.264
-I'm a pop star on the rise.
-Okay.


00:13:27.399 --> 00:13:28.954
[singer] So I wanna do
the album, you know.


00:13:29.037 --> 00:13:30.184
We can come in here
after midnight.


00:13:30.267 --> 00:13:31.805
I got the keys to the studio.


00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.634
-How's it going?
-Oh, good morning.


00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.871
Actually, it's literally
not. It's a bad morning.


00:13:36.007 --> 00:13:37.140
It's a very bad morning.


00:13:37.276 --> 00:13:38.879
Not for me, personally,
but for you.


00:13:39.015 --> 00:13:40.579
-Why, what happened?
-[inhales deeply]


00:13:40.715 --> 00:13:42.014
Trevor dumped Ella.


00:13:42.149 --> 00:13:43.847
And he already released
a song about it.


00:13:43.982 --> 00:13:46.457
<i>-Anna!
-Oh.</i>


00:13:46.592 --> 00:13:48.250
Yeah, and he dumped
her in a text.


00:13:48.385 --> 00:13:50.151
-Yeah, I got this.
-Toxic icon.


00:13:50.821 --> 00:13:53.458
I'll get in the booth, and
I'ma just lay it all down...


00:13:54.161 --> 00:13:55.542
[Anna] Okay, so
Trevor wrote a song.


00:13:55.625 --> 00:13:57.525
But I'm sure it's not
as bad as you think.


00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:59.399
It's called "Better
Than the Last One."


00:13:59.535 --> 00:14:00.870
It's about me.


00:14:01.005 --> 00:14:03.571
Okay, but that title, it
could be about anyone.


00:14:03.707 --> 00:14:05.870
It says, parentheses, "Ella."


00:14:06.006 --> 00:14:07.270
Let's just focus on the songs


00:14:07.406 --> 00:14:09.343
that you're gonna
perform on Saturday.


00:14:09.478 --> 00:14:10.738
Performing! Yay!


00:14:10.873 --> 00:14:15.046
I can't sing those songs.
I wrote them about Trevor.


00:14:15.181 --> 00:14:17.251
I put my heart and
soul into them.


00:14:17.386 --> 00:14:20.850
No, a 44-year-old Dutch music
producer wrote those songs.


00:14:21.586 --> 00:14:23.656
[Trevor] ♪ <i>She's
nothing like my ex</i> ♪


00:14:23.792 --> 00:14:25.320
This is a hit! This is...


00:14:25.456 --> 00:14:27.022
I can't even stop
moving my body.


00:14:27.158 --> 00:14:28.357
-Shh!
-Look, my chest


00:14:28.492 --> 00:14:29.852
-is just gyrating. I can't...
-Off!


00:14:30.526 --> 00:14:32.197
Oh, turn it off.
Turn... All right.


00:14:34.335 --> 00:14:36.498
What is that? Did you
learn that from Oprah?


00:14:36.633 --> 00:14:38.193
[student 1] Join the
Environmental Club.


00:14:38.306 --> 00:14:40.094
[student 2] Come over.
We have the best cookies.


00:14:40.177 --> 00:14:41.654
[Simon] Welcome to the
great Sunset Ridge Bake-Off.


00:14:41.737 --> 00:14:43.942
Shouldn't these be more
prominently featured?


00:14:44.077 --> 00:14:45.474
<i>Bon Appétit</i> literally profiled


00:14:45.609 --> 00:14:47.129
my dad's restaurant
for these pastries.


00:14:47.215 --> 00:14:50.077
I think they're nice
and prominent over here.


00:14:50.213 --> 00:14:51.452
Uh, they're gourmet.


00:14:51.588 --> 00:14:53.121
They're soggy-bottomed.


00:14:53.257 --> 00:14:56.419
You know what? I think I see
the perfect spot for yours.


00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:58.595
-Just...
-Dude!


00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.591
-Those were Gram's!
-Come on.


00:15:00.727 --> 00:15:05.895
You know what? I think I know
the perfect place to put this.


00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:08.136
You wouldn't dare.


00:15:08.272 --> 00:15:09.531
[sighs]


00:15:10.606 --> 00:15:12.468
-[gasps]
-Oh.


00:15:13.972 --> 00:15:15.542
Yeah. Perfect.


00:15:15.678 --> 00:15:16.938
Nice caramelization.


00:15:17.073 --> 00:15:19.479
Oh. Just...


00:15:19.614 --> 00:15:20.744
[students gasp]


00:15:20.879 --> 00:15:22.011
Oh, my God.


00:15:22.146 --> 00:15:23.882
[♪ "Oh!" playing]


00:15:24.017 --> 00:15:27.351
[mouthing words] Food fight!


00:15:28.491 --> 00:15:30.019
Food fight!


00:15:30.155 --> 00:15:32.829
-Oh, no!
-[screaming]


00:15:35.331 --> 00:15:37.733
[Harper's friend] They're
attacking us from above!


00:15:37.869 --> 00:15:39.935
[student 3] We need
the high ground!


00:15:41.471 --> 00:15:44.401
[clamoring]


00:15:46.039 --> 00:15:47.470
[student 3] On my signal!


00:15:48.975 --> 00:15:51.540
[distorted yelling]


00:15:55.718 --> 00:15:57.254
[Lily] Too far, Harper.


00:15:57.723 --> 00:15:59.615
Stop it! Put that down! Stop it.


00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.819
Give me that. Give me that.
Put that down. Stop it!


00:16:01.955 --> 00:16:03.425
No, not the strudel!


00:16:03.561 --> 00:16:05.796
Please! Or the tart.


00:16:14.939 --> 00:16:17.401
Stop it! That got
in my mouth! Hey!


00:16:19.703 --> 00:16:21.576
[Waldman] You want a
fight? Let's fight!


00:16:21.711 --> 00:16:25.145
[distorted clamoring]


00:16:25.979 --> 00:16:27.884
[distorted gasping]


00:16:32.555 --> 00:16:34.187
[gasping]


00:16:37.593 --> 00:16:39.625
[exhales deeply]


00:16:39.761 --> 00:16:41.392
Who started...


00:16:42.433 --> 00:16:43.559
the food fight?


00:16:45.868 --> 00:16:47.334
Congratulations, you two.


00:16:47.469 --> 00:16:50.104
You just got everybody in
here in-school suspension.


00:16:50.239 --> 00:16:52.035
-[students groaning]
-[student] Thanks a lot.


00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.107
Is this key lime pie?


00:16:54.242 --> 00:16:56.407
Yeah, I baked it
fresh this morning.


00:16:56.542 --> 00:16:58.197
Well, you gotta take me
to the emergency room


00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:01.017
because I'm very
allergic to key lime pie.


00:17:01.453 --> 00:17:05.450
[Anna, through headphones] ♪
<i>I just keep on coming back</i> ♪


00:17:05.585 --> 00:17:08.556
♪ <i>I'm your good
And I'm your...</i> ♪


00:17:08.692 --> 00:17:10.292
[Ella] Is this you?


00:17:10.428 --> 00:17:11.742
[through speakers] ♪ <i>Baby,
our love was made...</i> ♪


00:17:11.825 --> 00:17:13.323
Oh, uh...


00:17:13.459 --> 00:17:15.332
That's not supposed
to be in there.


00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:17.031
-Was it for Pink Slip?
-Hmm.


00:17:17.167 --> 00:17:19.298
I saw them at the
Troubadour last year.


00:17:21.203 --> 00:17:23.370
Could I sing your
song this weekend?


00:17:23.506 --> 00:17:24.766
Oh, no.


00:17:24.901 --> 00:17:26.456
You'll have way better stuff
than something I wrote.


00:17:26.539 --> 00:17:28.543
I wrote that after I
left Pink Slip anyway.


00:17:28.678 --> 00:17:31.447
Okay. I got this.


00:17:31.582 --> 00:17:32.782
Yes, you got this.


00:17:32.917 --> 00:17:34.782
Opening your world
tour at the Wiltern


00:17:34.917 --> 00:17:37.921
is a big show for you. Huge.


00:17:38.986 --> 00:17:40.553
For the both of us.


00:17:40.688 --> 00:17:42.508
The girls are struggling with
this transition, and just...


00:17:42.591 --> 00:17:45.261
just take it from a parent
who has been in your shoes.


00:17:45.396 --> 00:17:48.362
I know, Tess, between losing
Lily's mum and moving here...


00:17:48.498 --> 00:17:51.597
Yes, and being ripped away
from the home she grew up in.


00:17:51.732 --> 00:17:53.718
Oh, I'm sorry. Are we talking
about Lily or about Harper?


00:17:53.801 --> 00:17:54.836
Harp? Lily?


00:17:54.971 --> 00:17:56.189
[Tess] That is really annoying.


00:17:56.272 --> 00:17:57.788
-[Eric] No, it's just...
-Hey. What the...


00:17:57.871 --> 00:17:59.302
What's going on?


00:17:59.437 --> 00:18:00.674
-Darling...
-No one's hurt.


00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:01.877
I went to the school...


00:18:02.013 --> 00:18:03.253
Please let me just handle this.


00:18:04.346 --> 00:18:06.311
Anna, there's been
an incident at school


00:18:06.446 --> 00:18:07.951
between the girls.
It was really bad.


00:18:08.086 --> 00:18:12.218
-What bad? How bad? Oh...
-[Eric] I've got this.


00:18:12.354 --> 00:18:14.624
Girls, apologize to
each other now, please.


00:18:14.759 --> 00:18:16.958
Ooh, honey, forced apologies


00:18:17.094 --> 00:18:18.141
is never a way to
resolve conflict.


00:18:18.224 --> 00:18:19.690
-That...
-[Eric] But...


00:18:19.826 --> 00:18:22.394
We need to make space for
them to express how they feel.


00:18:22.863 --> 00:18:23.961
[exhales deeply]


00:18:24.097 --> 00:18:26.233
Harper, how do you feel?


00:18:27.604 --> 00:18:29.305
I feel...


00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.440
sorry.


00:18:31.039 --> 00:18:32.910
And, Lily, how do you feel?


00:18:33.545 --> 00:18:34.839
I feel... [sighs]


00:18:34.975 --> 00:18:35.774
...sorry too.


00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:36.910
That's great.


00:18:37.043 --> 00:18:38.444
-Great.
-See?


00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.268
Sorry that my future
stepsister is a complete twit.


00:18:40.351 --> 00:18:41.837
I'm sorry that my future
stepsister is a shallow idiot.


00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:43.777
-Oh, am I? Really?
-New plan!


00:18:43.912 --> 00:18:45.284
No more holding
space for feelings.


00:18:45.419 --> 00:18:47.019
You two are gonna
have a lovely time


00:18:47.154 --> 00:18:48.518
at my bachelorette tonight.


00:18:48.654 --> 00:18:49.976
You're gonna get along
because we're a family,


00:18:50.059 --> 00:18:51.357
and families love each other!


00:18:51.492 --> 00:18:53.127
And for that, Harper,
just for that look,


00:18:53.263 --> 00:18:56.566
you two earned yourself
a sleepover at Gram's.


00:18:56.701 --> 00:18:58.197
Huh? Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:18:58.333 --> 00:19:01.266
Why am I the punishment?
I'm the fun one.


00:19:01.402 --> 00:19:02.901
-I have board games.
-[Harper] Mom.


00:19:03.036 --> 00:19:04.304
I have Parcheesi.


00:19:04.439 --> 00:19:05.960
And you're gonna braid
each other's hair


00:19:06.043 --> 00:19:07.740
in a non
cultural-appropriating way


00:19:07.875 --> 00:19:08.676
and like it.


00:19:08.811 --> 00:19:10.212
What is Parcheesi?


00:19:10.347 --> 00:19:11.925
-[Tess] It's a game.
-[Eric] I'm not quite sure.


00:19:12.008 --> 00:19:13.331
You move around the
board. You shake the dice.


00:19:13.414 --> 00:19:14.979
You remember the
sound of the dice?


00:19:15.114 --> 00:19:15.914
Oh, it's amazing.


00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.117
You get these dice,


00:19:17.253 --> 00:19:18.516
and you shake 'em in your hand,


00:19:18.651 --> 00:19:20.214
-you move around the board.
-Oh, Grams.


00:19:20.349 --> 00:19:21.349
It's really fun.


00:19:21.484 --> 00:19:22.916
I also have Boggle!


00:19:23.052 --> 00:19:25.556
You stay on your side,
and I'll stay on mine.


00:19:26.596 --> 00:19:27.822
Gladly.


00:19:28.831 --> 00:19:30.000
Harper, look,


00:19:30.135 --> 00:19:31.481
I know you think I
don't get it, but I do.


00:19:31.564 --> 00:19:33.169
And it's still just
gonna be you and me.


00:19:33.304 --> 00:19:36.433
If you go to London, I'm
staying here with Grams.


00:19:36.569 --> 00:19:38.341
-She said it was cool.
-She what?


00:19:38.476 --> 00:19:42.310
Hey, Anna! Did you remove me
as Harper's secondary contact?


00:19:42.445 --> 00:19:45.078
Did you tell Harper that
she could stay here with you


00:19:45.213 --> 00:19:47.175
if we decided to move to London?


00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:48.310
[stammers]


00:19:48.715 --> 00:19:51.085
-Are you serious right now?
-Whoa. Are you serious?


00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:52.399
-[Tess] Okay, okay.
-Why are you...


00:19:52.482 --> 00:19:53.851
[Tess] What is serious


00:19:53.986 --> 00:19:57.254
is that you and Eric need to
keep the girls in Los Angeles.


00:19:57.390 --> 00:19:59.893
Lily just needs some guidance.


00:20:00.295 --> 00:20:01.855
The only guidance
I need from you


00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.429
is to show me to
the other bathroom.


00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:07.097
I'm very sorry, Lily.
I didn't know...


00:20:07.233 --> 00:20:08.299
You don't know anything


00:20:08.435 --> 00:20:10.438
about what I need or how I feel,


00:20:10.573 --> 00:20:13.203
or the fashion school back
home that I wanna go to.


00:20:13.339 --> 00:20:14.642
-[door slams]
-Oh!


00:20:15.011 --> 00:20:17.377
Yep. Just you and me, Mom.


00:20:17.911 --> 00:20:18.813
Great.


00:20:18.948 --> 00:20:20.415
[DJ] <i>Welcome, everyone,</i>


00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.877
<i>to the bachelorette
party of our girl, Anna.</i>


00:20:26.683 --> 00:20:28.921
[Harper groans] Mom, for real?


00:20:29.057 --> 00:20:30.786
[Harper] Why would you?


00:20:30.921 --> 00:20:33.086
-[Anna] Haven't changed.
-[Maddie] Not a bit.


00:20:33.789 --> 00:20:36.358
-[guest] Anna!
-It's so funny.


00:20:36.493 --> 00:20:37.194
[guest] Get it, girl!


00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:38.696
I remember that six-pack.


00:20:38.832 --> 00:20:40.821
-[Harper] Yeah, who is that?
-[Maddie] So handsome.


00:20:40.904 --> 00:20:42.769
[Peg] That is Jake.


00:20:43.238 --> 00:20:44.732
[Maddie] Your mom's first love.


00:20:44.868 --> 00:20:46.866
[Peg] And her first
ride on a motorcycle.


00:20:47.002 --> 00:20:49.812
I like to ride in
Jake's motorcycle.


00:20:49.947 --> 00:20:51.147
-Okay.
-[guests chuckle]


00:20:51.282 --> 00:20:53.308
[Maddie] Jake also
had a thing for Tess.


00:20:53.444 --> 00:20:54.679
[Harper] For Grams?


00:20:54.814 --> 00:20:56.563
All right, okay. Enough
humiliation for the night.


00:20:56.646 --> 00:20:58.484
[♪ Rock music playing]


00:21:11.059 --> 00:21:14.336
Harper, baby, I
made you a plate.


00:21:14.472 --> 00:21:17.030
Here you go. You're too
young to be sad. Come on.


00:21:17.165 --> 00:21:19.334
Well, being young is
overrated, Mama P.


00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:20.506
Eat. You'll be fine.


00:21:21.376 --> 00:21:23.839
[Mama P exclaims] Use the tongs.


00:21:29.554 --> 00:21:30.912
[sighs]


00:21:37.892 --> 00:21:39.129
[sighs]


00:21:43.594 --> 00:21:46.268
Lily? Mind if I join you?


00:21:50.306 --> 00:21:52.807
You know, Anna lost her father


00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:56.069
around the same age that
you lost your mother.


00:21:57.746 --> 00:22:01.077
And then she had to deal
with my wedding to Ryan.


00:22:01.212 --> 00:22:02.542
Cool.


00:22:03.344 --> 00:22:07.421
And then you add to that
the complications of moving.


00:22:08.485 --> 00:22:09.522
I'm here for you.


00:22:11.454 --> 00:22:12.822
Sincerely.


00:22:15.992 --> 00:22:18.359
With all due
respect, Dr. Coleman,


00:22:18.895 --> 00:22:21.095
you're not my gran
or my therapist.


00:22:21.231 --> 00:22:23.437
So, while I get your motive
for keeping us in LA,


00:22:24.172 --> 00:22:25.406
I don't need your help.


00:22:29.737 --> 00:22:30.938
[exhales sharply]


00:22:31.073 --> 00:22:33.347
[Anna] Oh, no. We
used to be so cool.


00:22:33.483 --> 00:22:36.176
-Hey, I'm still cool.
-I look amazing.


00:22:36.312 --> 00:22:38.169
You're very cool. That
song you sent me was sick.


00:22:38.252 --> 00:22:39.385
-Yeah.
-Thank you.


00:22:39.521 --> 00:22:41.148
I wish I had more time to write.


00:22:41.284 --> 00:22:43.218
But now all I do is listen
to parenting podcasts.


00:22:43.353 --> 00:22:46.620
Well, I'm sorry for ruining
your exciting rock star life.


00:22:46.756 --> 00:22:48.187
Harper, wait. I was just...


00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:50.266
Wait, I wasn't serious.


00:22:50.401 --> 00:22:52.435
Look, I gave up
performing, but I have you.


00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:56.036
-[Harper] Enjoy your party.
-[Anna] You can't leave.


00:22:56.439 --> 00:22:58.239
I don't think I
belong in here, Grams.


00:22:58.375 --> 00:22:59.586
Let me handle
this. I've got you.


00:22:59.669 --> 00:23:01.101
-[Anna] Harper!
-Anna,


00:23:01.236 --> 00:23:03.703
honey, you just need
to pause and reframe.


00:23:03.839 --> 00:23:05.246
-Thanks, Mom.
-What?


00:23:05.382 --> 00:23:06.876
-What did I do?
-I was handling it.


00:23:07.011 --> 00:23:08.662
And you completely
undermine me as a parent.


00:23:08.745 --> 00:23:09.843
I was trying to help you.


00:23:09.978 --> 00:23:11.063
Well, your help isn't helpful.


00:23:11.146 --> 00:23:12.980
Well, that's not
very nice to say.


00:23:13.116 --> 00:23:15.852
Can the great and
mysterious Madame Jen


00:23:15.987 --> 00:23:18.494
interest you ladies
in a psychic reading?


00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.690
[chuckles] No.
Thank you very much,


00:23:21.826 --> 00:23:23.632
but, um, right now is not the...


00:23:23.767 --> 00:23:24.958
Time?


00:23:25.094 --> 00:23:26.829
-It's just not really our...
-Thing?


00:23:26.965 --> 00:23:29.538
This will all be over
soon, if you just...


00:23:30.408 --> 00:23:32.173
-Go with it.
-Go with it. Yes, exactly.


00:23:32.308 --> 00:23:33.508
-Come on in. Yes. Yes.
-No. No.


00:23:33.641 --> 00:23:35.136
-Come.
-Okay, I'm coming. Here we go.


00:23:35.271 --> 00:23:36.495
-Anybody else interested?
-Let's try this out.


00:23:36.578 --> 00:23:38.098
I do discounts for
bigger groups. Okay?


00:23:38.183 --> 00:23:39.847
Okay. That's fine. That's good.


00:23:39.982 --> 00:23:41.247
[door locks]


00:23:41.383 --> 00:23:42.843
And that's how I lost my spot


00:23:42.978 --> 00:23:44.417
at the Larchmont
Farmers' Market.


00:23:44.553 --> 00:23:46.982
But I did get a
table by the lids


00:23:47.117 --> 00:23:49.556
and free milk counter
inside of the Starbucks.


00:23:49.691 --> 00:23:53.626
So, I am a life coach,
but I also do Reiki.


00:23:53.762 --> 00:23:55.897
If you notice, I have
several business cards,


00:23:56.033 --> 00:23:57.100
because I actually have


00:23:57.236 --> 00:23:59.562
a business-card-making business.


00:23:59.698 --> 00:24:00.781
So, that's the card for that.


00:24:00.864 --> 00:24:02.269
Uh, I can put quotes on there


00:24:02.405 --> 00:24:04.264
that I can just make up for you.


00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:06.736
If you want something
inspirational, for example,


00:24:06.872 --> 00:24:09.143
I can make up a
quote like, um...


00:24:09.279 --> 00:24:11.538
"Live your life... [stammers]


00:24:11.674 --> 00:24:12.775
Gosh dang it."


00:24:12.911 --> 00:24:14.231
-Okay.
-[Madame Jen] So, here's...


00:24:14.353 --> 00:24:19.055
And-And-And I'm gonna
read your palms now.


00:24:19.190 --> 00:24:20.554
-'Cause that's...
-[Tess] Really?


00:24:22.058 --> 00:24:23.058
[Madame Jen sighs]


00:24:23.194 --> 00:24:27.695
Okay. And there they go. Yes.


00:24:28.398 --> 00:24:30.190
[mumbles] Eenie,
meeney, miney...


00:24:30.759 --> 00:24:32.225
[sniffs] Hmm.


00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:35.498
Okay. It smells like
you had some appetizers.


00:24:35.634 --> 00:24:36.666
-Were they good?
-Good.


00:24:36.801 --> 00:24:38.233
-Good. Yes.
-Yeah. Yes.


00:24:38.769 --> 00:24:40.376
And did you have any, Mom?


00:24:41.811 --> 00:24:45.171
-Um, no. Mm-mmm. No. I didn't.
-I'm... No. No. Didn't...


00:24:45.307 --> 00:24:46.947
-'Cause I paid for them.
-I paid for them.


00:24:47.080 --> 00:24:50.177
-It's a wedding. Okay.
-[babbles] Okay. Okay, okay.


00:24:50.312 --> 00:24:54.291
Your life lines. It...
It's like they've...


00:24:56.819 --> 00:24:58.628
intersected before.


00:24:59.131 --> 00:25:00.589
-How strange.
-Really?


00:25:00.724 --> 00:25:01.957
[Madame Jen stammers]


00:25:02.092 --> 00:25:05.458
You've walked in
each other's path.


00:25:06.428 --> 00:25:11.973
It's like a crazy
path-cross that you've done.


00:25:12.108 --> 00:25:14.377
[gasps, straining]


00:25:17.041 --> 00:25:18.742
[distorted] You've
learned a lesson.


00:25:18.878 --> 00:25:21.175
A lesson that may
serve you again.


00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:22.978
-Okay. That's enough.
-Thank you. Okay.


00:25:23.113 --> 00:25:24.634
[Tess] We'll give
these to my neighbors.


00:25:24.717 --> 00:25:26.053
[normal] I'm onto
something here.


00:25:26.189 --> 00:25:28.987
One more thing. [sighs]


00:25:29.123 --> 00:25:31.722
Right over there is a QR code
that you can tip me with.


00:25:31.857 --> 00:25:33.923
Any amount is
appreciated. Really.


00:25:34.058 --> 00:25:35.696
I didn't know I
could do that voice.


00:25:35.831 --> 00:25:38.460
-Nice prank. Ha-ha.
-Yeah, we know what you did.


00:25:38.596 --> 00:25:39.629
What did I do?


00:25:39.765 --> 00:25:41.263
What do you mean? The psychic.


00:25:41.399 --> 00:25:43.282
-Yeah. Telling her about...
-[Mama P] What... Okay, okay.


00:25:43.365 --> 00:25:45.903
You think I'd rather
solve your problem


00:25:46.038 --> 00:25:49.269
than deal with my
booming culinary empire.


00:25:49.404 --> 00:25:52.614
♪ <i>I just thought Think about</i> ♪


00:25:52.749 --> 00:25:54.408
♪ <i>All the things you
can And can't get</i> ♪


00:25:54.544 --> 00:25:56.743
-I'm following you because...
-You're happy here, so...


00:25:56.879 --> 00:25:58.045
Are you the psychic?


00:25:58.181 --> 00:25:59.408
I need you to look
into my future


00:25:59.491 --> 00:26:00.770
and tell me where
we're going to live.


00:26:00.853 --> 00:26:03.592
Oh. Cool Gen Z talking to me.


00:26:03.728 --> 00:26:05.956
If it's not London, I need
you to alter my destiny.


00:26:06.091 --> 00:26:08.259
And I literally have
to stay in Los Angeles,


00:26:08.394 --> 00:26:09.430
so, if there's...


00:26:09.566 --> 00:26:11.368
Well, that's not
really how it works.


00:26:12.169 --> 00:26:13.799
Well, how does it work?


00:26:14.868 --> 00:26:19.303
Girls, follow my
aura. [chuckles]


00:26:19.438 --> 00:26:21.801
Boop. Beep.


00:26:21.937 --> 00:26:23.504
[mimics pushing buttons]


00:26:23.639 --> 00:26:24.859
[Madame Jen] You don't have
a lot of lines in your hands,


00:26:24.942 --> 00:26:26.093
so it makes it harder for me.


00:26:26.176 --> 00:26:28.143
You two are called to be family.


00:26:28.278 --> 00:26:30.948
-Yeah, right.
-[scoffs] Don't remind me.


00:26:32.783 --> 00:26:34.314
A lesson for you all.


00:26:36.786 --> 00:26:38.318
I see it now.


00:26:38.863 --> 00:26:40.056
[gasps]


00:26:43.094 --> 00:26:45.060
Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:26:45.195 --> 00:26:47.997
to reach the place
where you belong.


00:26:48.132 --> 00:26:50.098
Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:26:50.233 --> 00:26:52.635
to reach the place
where you belong.


00:26:53.204 --> 00:26:55.301
Change the hearts
you know are wrong...


00:26:55.437 --> 00:26:57.639
Why is she rhyming
like a bridge troll?


00:26:58.241 --> 00:27:00.944
Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:27:01.079 --> 00:27:03.847
to reach the place
where you belong.


00:27:03.983 --> 00:27:06.350
-Change the hearts...
-Earthquake.


00:27:06.485 --> 00:27:08.018
Earthquake?


00:27:08.153 --> 00:27:10.889
-[rumbling]
-[music in venue slows down]


00:27:13.888 --> 00:27:15.124
[rumbling stops]


00:27:17.025 --> 00:27:18.929
[distorted yelling]


00:27:19.064 --> 00:27:21.127
[singer, normal]
♪ <i>Here and now</i> ♪


00:27:21.262 --> 00:27:23.000
[slow] ♪<i> Here and now</i> ♪


00:27:31.808 --> 00:27:33.010
Did you feel that?


00:27:34.375 --> 00:27:37.080
Yeah, I... It must
be the dancing.


00:27:37.615 --> 00:27:39.017
Yeah, right.


00:27:39.152 --> 00:27:41.032
We're just freaking
ourselves out for no reason.


00:27:41.119 --> 00:27:43.483
-Yeah. It's just in our heads.
-Right.


00:27:43.618 --> 00:27:45.555
[radio announcer] <i>With
your surf forecast...</i>


00:27:45.691 --> 00:27:47.224
All cozy and tucked in?


00:27:47.360 --> 00:27:49.328
<i>Fearless prediction for
the full moon tonight...</i>


00:27:49.463 --> 00:27:50.733
[exhales sharply]


00:27:51.135 --> 00:27:52.364
You need anything?


00:27:52.834 --> 00:27:54.361
What more could I possibly need?


00:27:54.496 --> 00:27:56.533
[Harper] How about
sleeping in our own beds


00:27:56.668 --> 00:27:57.699
in our own rooms?


00:27:57.835 --> 00:27:59.476
-Hmm.
-Hmm.


00:28:01.046 --> 00:28:02.270
Sweet dreams.


00:28:03.543 --> 00:28:04.841
[Tess scoffs]


00:28:04.976 --> 00:28:06.082
-Teenagers.
-[Anna sighs]


00:28:06.217 --> 00:28:07.513
[Anna] I was one once.


00:28:07.649 --> 00:28:09.385
[Tess] Yeah, so was I. Twice.


00:28:09.521 --> 00:28:11.154
-[Tess] Night.
-[Anna] Night. Love you.


00:28:11.289 --> 00:28:12.417
[Tess] Love you too, honey.


00:28:12.552 --> 00:28:14.216
[thunder rumbles]


00:28:32.768 --> 00:28:35.105
[Madame Jen] <i>Change the
hearts you know are wrong</i>


00:28:35.241 --> 00:28:37.976
<i>to reach the place
where you belong.</i>


00:28:38.112 --> 00:28:40.209
<i>Change the hearts
you know are wrong</i>


00:28:40.345 --> 00:28:42.446
<i>to reach the place
where you belong.</i>


00:28:42.581 --> 00:28:45.016
[alarm ringing]


00:28:48.219 --> 00:28:50.791
[Harper groans] <i>I
don't have an alarm.</i>


00:28:52.994 --> 00:28:54.797
[Harper] <i>Why do my
hands look so dry?</i>


00:28:54.933 --> 00:28:56.126
[grunts]


00:28:56.896 --> 00:28:58.260
[Harper] <i>Why am I so tired?</i>


00:29:00.567 --> 00:29:01.828
[Harper] <i>Mom?</i>


00:29:01.963 --> 00:29:03.236
[Anna] Mom?


00:29:04.005 --> 00:29:05.498
-[Harper] <i>Grams?</i>
-[Anna] Grams?


00:29:09.138 --> 00:29:13.311
Grams. Grams, are you okay?


00:29:14.014 --> 00:29:16.945
Why are you bloody
waking me up for?


00:29:17.080 --> 00:29:19.120
-Are you mad?
-Mad?


00:29:19.489 --> 00:29:20.650
Why do I sound like this?


00:29:20.786 --> 00:29:22.284
[Anna] Sound like what?


00:29:22.918 --> 00:29:24.319
American!


00:29:26.187 --> 00:29:28.261
[gasping, grunting]


00:29:28.397 --> 00:29:30.798
Oh. Good. Mom.


00:29:31.532 --> 00:29:32.595
What was that?


00:29:32.730 --> 00:29:35.329
Ow! Oh. Ow!


00:29:35.465 --> 00:29:37.970
-[sighs]
-[Harper] Lily, are you okay?


00:29:38.605 --> 00:29:40.434
I'm not Lily.


00:29:46.073 --> 00:29:47.342
Are you Harper?


00:29:48.712 --> 00:29:50.042
No.


00:29:50.178 --> 00:29:54.285
No. No. No, no, no.


00:29:54.921 --> 00:29:58.452
-I'm bloody decomposing!
-Oh, my.


00:29:58.921 --> 00:30:01.554
[both screaming]


00:30:02.793 --> 00:30:04.130
[both gasp]


00:30:04.266 --> 00:30:05.159
Harper?


00:30:05.294 --> 00:30:07.460
-Oh, my God.
-[Harper] Whoa.


00:30:07.596 --> 00:30:09.015
-What is happening?
-[Harper] I know.


00:30:09.098 --> 00:30:10.733
It's me, Harp. It's Mom.


00:30:10.869 --> 00:30:12.303
What are you saying?


00:30:12.439 --> 00:30:15.106
So if you're me and I'm you,
then... then who is that?


00:30:15.841 --> 00:30:17.273
I'm Grandma, sweetheart.


00:30:19.645 --> 00:30:21.277
[screams]


00:30:23.145 --> 00:30:25.648
Oh, my gosh! I've died.


00:30:25.783 --> 00:30:28.020
I killed myself!


00:30:28.155 --> 00:30:30.820
She just has crevices
all over her face.


00:30:30.955 --> 00:30:32.592
Look at the crevices.


00:30:32.728 --> 00:30:34.527
My hands look like doll hands.


00:30:34.662 --> 00:30:36.497
My butt feels so high.


00:30:36.633 --> 00:30:37.891
I think I just peed a little.


00:30:38.026 --> 00:30:39.161
[Harper] Oh, no.


00:30:39.296 --> 00:30:42.699
My face feels so
thirsty and dry.


00:30:42.835 --> 00:30:45.166
My face is perfect.


00:30:45.301 --> 00:30:47.434
My face looks like a Birkin bag


00:30:47.570 --> 00:30:51.274
that's been left out
in the sun to rot.


00:30:51.808 --> 00:30:52.808
Why?


00:30:52.912 --> 00:30:54.508
Why do I have to pee again?


00:30:54.643 --> 00:30:57.077
This is so much weirder
than the last time.


00:30:57.213 --> 00:30:58.915
Last time? What last time?


00:30:59.050 --> 00:31:00.616
How come you never told me?


00:31:00.751 --> 00:31:02.875
[Harper] We never told anyone,
sweetheart. Overnight oats.


00:31:02.958 --> 00:31:04.485
Now let's just
pause and reframe.


00:31:04.620 --> 00:31:06.553
No. I didn't want to be
a part of this family


00:31:06.689 --> 00:31:09.828
and now I'm part of
some dodgy family curse?


00:31:09.963 --> 00:31:11.832
-And I'm the eldest?
-Mom.


00:31:11.967 --> 00:31:15.336
And where are her
lips? She has no lips!


00:31:15.471 --> 00:31:16.471
Where did they go?


00:31:16.573 --> 00:31:17.798
[Anna] How do we fix this?


00:31:18.601 --> 00:31:20.281
Well, you know, last
time, we switched back


00:31:20.406 --> 00:31:22.709
when we saw things from
the other's perspective.


00:31:22.844 --> 00:31:23.974
[Lily] Should we hold hands?


00:31:24.109 --> 00:31:25.291
-Hold my hands.
-Well, we can...


00:31:25.374 --> 00:31:27.149
-Just... [clears throat]
-Yeah.


00:31:27.819 --> 00:31:29.577
I know I've been
hard on you and Eric,


00:31:29.712 --> 00:31:32.351
but I can now see that
you're doing the right thing.


00:31:32.487 --> 00:31:38.189
And, Mom, you have always done
so much for me, and I see you.


00:31:42.827 --> 00:31:44.296
I see you.


00:31:44.431 --> 00:31:45.817
-Are you really seeing me?
-Mm-hmm. I really see you.


00:31:45.900 --> 00:31:47.233
Because I don't feel anything.


00:31:47.368 --> 00:31:49.771
You have no idea how hard
I'm seeing you right now.


00:31:49.907 --> 00:31:51.568
-[Tess] One, two, three.
-[Anna] ...three.


00:31:52.271 --> 00:31:53.937
[groans] Girls,
that doesn't work.


00:31:54.073 --> 00:31:55.536
Yeah, we tried that last time.


00:31:56.743 --> 00:31:58.174
Looking like this


00:31:58.310 --> 00:32:01.079
is why people like
you become shut-ins,


00:32:01.215 --> 00:32:03.785
and what's with this
accent? "Tomato."


00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:05.787
Is that what you
think I sound like?


00:32:05.922 --> 00:32:07.138
[in British accent]
Oh, my God, yes.


00:32:07.221 --> 00:32:09.122
Of course this is
what you sound like.


00:32:09.257 --> 00:32:10.603
-Let's go to Erewhon...
-I do not sound like that.


00:32:10.686 --> 00:32:12.958
I've never said that.
I don't even know...


00:32:13.094 --> 00:32:14.892
Then I need to call
my energy healer


00:32:15.028 --> 00:32:16.359
because I need a chakra reset.


00:32:16.494 --> 00:32:18.801
-That's what you sound like.
-The healer.


00:32:19.732 --> 00:32:20.862
Madame Jen.


00:32:21.231 --> 00:32:22.563
I thought she was a psychic.


00:32:22.699 --> 00:32:24.806
Ow. I thought she did
sound baths for dogs.


00:32:24.941 --> 00:32:26.574
I thought she was
a water sommelier.


00:32:26.710 --> 00:32:27.941
She did try to sell me knives.


00:32:28.077 --> 00:32:30.471
[stammers] What? No,
well, whatever she is,


00:32:30.607 --> 00:32:33.447
we have to find her,
but until then...


00:32:33.582 --> 00:32:34.749
"Until then" what?


00:32:34.885 --> 00:32:36.676
Last time we convinced everyone


00:32:36.811 --> 00:32:38.568
that we were each other
until we switched back.


00:32:38.651 --> 00:32:42.253
Oh, brilliant. So how are we
supposed to pull that off?


00:32:42.389 --> 00:32:45.157
Well, panicking is not
going to help anyone!


00:32:45.292 --> 00:32:46.852
-I need you to get dressed.
-This sucks!


00:32:46.961 --> 00:32:48.928
-Go. Go get...
-No! Stop.


00:32:49.064 --> 00:32:50.892
Bye, girls. It's
going to be great.


00:32:51.027 --> 00:32:52.429
Look, Mom.


00:32:52.564 --> 00:32:54.219
I kept it totally together
in front of the girls,


00:32:54.302 --> 00:32:57.202
but I have to be honest, I
am freaking out right now!


00:32:57.337 --> 00:32:59.602
That was you keeping
it totally together?


00:32:59.738 --> 00:33:00.574
Yes!


00:33:00.709 --> 00:33:02.273
No, no. Just checking.


00:33:03.108 --> 00:33:04.307
[Lily] Aura photographer.


00:33:04.443 --> 00:33:06.315
Hmm. Twenty percent
off on her Etsy shop.


00:33:06.451 --> 00:33:07.451
I can't get married.


00:33:07.544 --> 00:33:08.949
I haven't even had
a boyfriend yet.


00:33:09.084 --> 00:33:10.817
We have to switch
back to our bodies.


00:33:11.352 --> 00:33:15.291
At least your body didn't
wake up with arthritis.


00:33:15.426 --> 00:33:16.816
It's disconnected.


00:33:16.951 --> 00:33:18.572
I guess her life coaching
business went bust.


00:33:18.655 --> 00:33:20.528
I'm supposed to get
married this weekend.


00:33:20.663 --> 00:33:22.030
[Tess] What are these?


00:33:22.165 --> 00:33:24.461
And how many puffer
jackets does someone need?


00:33:24.596 --> 00:33:27.168
-Hmm. Reiki master. [gasps]
-What? What'd you find?


00:33:27.737 --> 00:33:31.733
I bent down and didn't toot.


00:33:32.569 --> 00:33:34.272
Youth really is
wasted on the young.


00:33:34.407 --> 00:33:38.806
And what's with the old
tissues in every pocket?


00:33:38.942 --> 00:33:40.216
Explain.


00:33:40.351 --> 00:33:41.110
[dial tone]


00:33:41.246 --> 00:33:43.214
No answer at Reiki. Now what?


00:33:43.350 --> 00:33:44.977
Did you try her vegan
meat loaf truck?


00:33:45.113 --> 00:33:47.136
They don't have a number,
and they only use DoorDash,


00:33:47.219 --> 00:33:48.368
and I don't know how to do that.


00:33:48.451 --> 00:33:52.191
I look Eileen Fisher years old.


00:33:53.058 --> 00:33:55.360
I'm literally my mother.


00:33:55.495 --> 00:33:57.863
I'm going to need therapy
for the rest of my life


00:33:57.998 --> 00:33:59.264
and not the kind from Grams.


00:33:59.400 --> 00:34:02.504
Like the real kind that
you have to pay for.


00:34:02.973 --> 00:34:04.806
[groans] Why does
anyone wear these?


00:34:04.942 --> 00:34:06.907
Did she say anything,
like a fortune?


00:34:07.043 --> 00:34:09.943
No, but maybe she
told the girls.


00:34:10.079 --> 00:34:11.710
[Harper] Did the
psychic say anything


00:34:11.846 --> 00:34:13.311
to you about a fortune?


00:34:13.446 --> 00:34:15.347
It could be the key to
getting out of this.


00:34:16.217 --> 00:34:17.484
-Wait, she did, right?
-She did.


00:34:17.619 --> 00:34:18.821
What was it?


00:34:18.956 --> 00:34:21.021
"Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:34:21.156 --> 00:34:23.486
to reach the place
where you belong."


00:34:23.621 --> 00:34:26.218
[gasps] That's about our
parents getting married.


00:34:26.353 --> 00:34:28.830
LA. London.


00:34:28.966 --> 00:34:31.859
As teenagers, we have no power.


00:34:31.994 --> 00:34:36.939
No say in whether we move
or stay, but as adults...


00:34:38.305 --> 00:34:40.199
Mom, she didn't
say anything to us!


00:34:40.334 --> 00:34:41.170
[screams]


00:34:41.306 --> 00:34:43.874
-[Harper grunting]
-Oh.


00:34:44.009 --> 00:34:45.608
Whoa. Anna. Anna!


00:34:45.743 --> 00:34:47.529
You do not hit me. I am
your mother, young lady.


00:34:47.612 --> 00:34:50.117
-So, what do you say?
-[Harper] Well, then...


00:34:50.253 --> 00:34:52.652
-[Harper] It's not working!
-We need a plan.


00:34:52.788 --> 00:34:53.951
[Lily] Not my fault!


00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:56.388
-DK doughnuts!
-[Harper] She'll love those.


00:34:56.523 --> 00:34:58.403
-Harper, got 'em.
-[Harper] I... I'll love them.


00:34:58.523 --> 00:35:00.661
Hey, girls. How
was the sleepover?


00:35:00.796 --> 00:35:02.325
-Good.
-Very good.


00:35:02.461 --> 00:35:03.999
-We did teenager stuff.
-Very good.


00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:07.132
[Tess] So here's our plan.


00:35:07.268 --> 00:35:09.635
First, these
clothes are rubbish.


00:35:09.771 --> 00:35:10.938
I just can't.


00:35:11.074 --> 00:35:15.472
Can you just give
me five minutes?


00:35:28.185 --> 00:35:29.490
-What?
-Oh, no.


00:35:29.625 --> 00:35:31.057
How? Why?


00:35:31.193 --> 00:35:32.507
[Tess] <i>You're in
your mum's body,</i>


00:35:32.590 --> 00:35:34.729
so all you have to
do is tell my dad


00:35:34.864 --> 00:35:36.631
you don't love him anymore.


00:35:36.766 --> 00:35:37.896
Wedding is off. Done.


00:35:38.031 --> 00:35:40.794
Whoa. Got some bangs.


00:35:40.929 --> 00:35:42.999
-What did you do to my hair?
-I fixed it.


00:35:43.135 --> 00:35:44.268
And you're welcome.


00:35:44.404 --> 00:35:45.805
-It's called a fringe.
-Fixed it.


00:35:45.941 --> 00:35:47.239
You don't seriously think


00:35:47.375 --> 00:35:48.953
you're going to my
work dressed like this.


00:35:49.036 --> 00:35:50.461
Take that off. You're
going to get me fired.


00:35:50.544 --> 00:35:51.633
-What'd you do to my hair?
-I straightened it.


00:35:51.716 --> 00:35:52.949
You never wash your hair.


00:35:53.084 --> 00:35:54.499
No, I don't. The ocean
washes it for me.


00:35:54.582 --> 00:35:56.776
[Tess] <i>Obviously, the
wedding can't happen.</i>


00:35:56.912 --> 00:35:58.368
It's Friday. We only
have till Sunday.


00:35:58.451 --> 00:36:00.255
We gotta do some
serious sabotage.


00:36:00.391 --> 00:36:02.915
<i>The immigration interview,
the rehearsal lunch.</i>


00:36:03.051 --> 00:36:06.825
Then what if we cancel
all the wedding stuff?


00:36:06.961 --> 00:36:08.894
The cake, place, people.


00:36:09.030 --> 00:36:10.495
Yes, and all we have to do


00:36:10.630 --> 00:36:13.200
is convince our parents
that they are incompatible.


00:36:13.335 --> 00:36:15.630
Which should not be hard
because my mom obviously


00:36:15.766 --> 00:36:18.137
should not be with some
wannabe Gordon Ramsay.


00:36:18.272 --> 00:36:20.537
Well, my father
doesn't want to be


00:36:20.673 --> 00:36:24.977
with some wannabe Valley
Village rocker mom.


00:36:25.113 --> 00:36:27.716
I quite like this, sexy tiger.


00:36:27.852 --> 00:36:28.981
-Doughnut!
-It's, um...


00:36:29.117 --> 00:36:30.447
It's an American superstition


00:36:30.583 --> 00:36:32.005
that it's bad luck for
the bride and groom


00:36:32.088 --> 00:36:33.820
to kiss before
they say I do so...


00:36:33.955 --> 00:36:35.748
Really? For how long?


00:36:35.883 --> 00:36:37.957
For a long time.
A long, long time.


00:36:38.093 --> 00:36:39.561
-Really?
-Yeah. Also, uh...


00:36:39.696 --> 00:36:40.927
no touching hands.


00:36:41.063 --> 00:36:42.326
No touching at all. [chuckles]


00:36:42.462 --> 00:36:44.161
No gazing into each other's eyes


00:36:44.297 --> 00:36:46.527
because it's gross. Um, yeah.


00:36:46.663 --> 00:36:48.093
-How odd.
-For maximum luck.


00:36:48.229 --> 00:36:51.430
[Tess] And finally, we
must be convincing as them


00:36:51.566 --> 00:36:52.899
until we break them up.


00:36:55.403 --> 00:36:56.336
[Ryan] Lily?


00:36:56.472 --> 00:36:57.541
-What?
-Yeah?


00:36:58.939 --> 00:37:00.713
Did you just take
Tess's calcium?


00:37:00.848 --> 00:37:02.084
[Lily] Mmm.


00:37:06.656 --> 00:37:07.881
[Tess] Mmm.


00:37:08.757 --> 00:37:09.982
Bone health.


00:37:11.991 --> 00:37:13.226
You need those.


00:37:13.362 --> 00:37:14.844
-You need those.
-Yes, I'll be taking them.


00:37:14.927 --> 00:37:16.331
Okay.


00:37:16.466 --> 00:37:18.076
-You need to take those.
-Give me the doughnut back.


00:37:18.159 --> 00:37:19.619
-No. You're very diabetic.
-[Eric] Okay, girls.


00:37:19.702 --> 00:37:21.193
Let's crack on.


00:37:21.796 --> 00:37:23.261
-[all] Oh.
-[Harper] Um...


00:37:23.397 --> 00:37:26.004
Well, actually, uh, Lily and
I aren't feeling very well.


00:37:26.140 --> 00:37:27.267
We think it might be a...


00:37:27.402 --> 00:37:28.339
My throat.


00:37:28.475 --> 00:37:29.903
...smart decision to stay home.


00:37:30.038 --> 00:37:32.580
This has nothing to do
with your detention?


00:37:32.715 --> 00:37:34.249
Oh. Uh...


00:37:34.384 --> 00:37:37.453
Well, you wouldn't want
me to go to school sick,


00:37:37.588 --> 00:37:38.588
would you, Mom?


00:37:38.687 --> 00:37:40.012
Hmm.


00:37:40.891 --> 00:37:41.953
You don't feel sick to me.


00:37:42.689 --> 00:37:44.951
Does she look sick to
you, Grams? I mean, Mom?


00:37:46.060 --> 00:37:48.687
No. They look fine.


00:37:48.822 --> 00:37:50.022
You have your client Ella's


00:37:50.157 --> 00:37:51.857
huge<i> Rolling Stone</i>
photo shoot today


00:37:51.992 --> 00:37:53.466
and your immigration interview.


00:37:53.601 --> 00:37:56.035
Don't you need a little
bit of help with that, hmm?


00:37:56.171 --> 00:37:57.768
Of course she needs your help.


00:37:57.904 --> 00:37:58.904
[scoffs]


00:37:59.007 --> 00:38:00.307
Right? Kids these days.


00:38:00.442 --> 00:38:02.235
They'll say anything
to get out of school.


00:38:02.371 --> 00:38:04.495
-All right. Come on. Let's go.
-Go on. And make good choices.


00:38:04.578 --> 00:38:06.944
-See you at the dance studio!
-Bye! What?


00:38:07.080 --> 00:38:08.341
Dance studio?


00:38:09.177 --> 00:38:11.276
Let's go. Change at the
club. I've got your bag.


00:38:11.412 --> 00:38:12.346
Change?


00:38:12.482 --> 00:38:13.347
This is the finals.


00:38:13.483 --> 00:38:14.484
Welcome, everybody,


00:38:14.620 --> 00:38:17.055
to the Westside
Pickleball Championship.


00:38:17.458 --> 00:38:20.052
Yeah. You have your
championship today.


00:38:21.031 --> 00:38:22.228
I think you're gonna be late.


00:38:22.363 --> 00:38:24.693
Late? Yes! Yeah,
I'm gonna be late.


00:38:24.829 --> 00:38:26.187
[dance instructor]
<i>Okay, newlyweds,</i>


00:38:26.270 --> 00:38:28.871
<i>you just made your
grand entrance</i>


00:38:29.006 --> 00:38:30.537
<i>into the wedding reception.</i>


00:38:30.673 --> 00:38:35.144
The lights begin to dim. And
a five, six, seven, Eric.


00:38:36.280 --> 00:38:39.346
-[instructor] Beth, no.
-Oh, right. Like a bull.


00:38:40.344 --> 00:38:41.380
[instructor] Yes!


00:38:41.516 --> 00:38:44.118
-Charging. It's a bull. Yes.
-Stallion.


00:38:44.254 --> 00:38:46.453
Get it, groom. Big
stallion energy.


00:38:46.588 --> 00:38:48.307
-[Beth] It's a bull, though.
-[instructor] All right.


00:38:48.390 --> 00:38:49.790
-[instructor] So look at him.
-What?


00:38:49.919 --> 00:38:50.942
[instructor] Eye
contact, come on.


00:38:51.025 --> 00:38:52.453
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:38:52.588 --> 00:38:54.627
Tango is your pelvis.


00:38:54.762 --> 00:38:56.995
[commentator 1] Pickleball.
It's a sport like tennis


00:38:57.131 --> 00:38:58.430
but it is pathetic.


00:38:58.566 --> 00:39:00.299
Tennis for lazy people,
that's what it is.


00:39:00.435 --> 00:39:02.002
It's like tennis but
for non athletes.


00:39:02.137 --> 00:39:03.502
It's a bunch of old nutters


00:39:03.637 --> 00:39:05.403
with giant paddles
chasing a Wiffle ball.


00:39:05.539 --> 00:39:07.539
It's not bloody
Wimbledon, is it?


00:39:08.437 --> 00:39:09.437
Here we go.


00:39:10.071 --> 00:39:12.881
-That's yours!
-Okay. That was so fast.


00:39:13.016 --> 00:39:14.313
[shrieks] Oh, so aggressive!


00:39:14.449 --> 00:39:16.475
-What was that?
-She almost hit me!


00:39:16.977 --> 00:39:18.812
-[Eric] Oh.
-[Anna] Okay.


00:39:19.348 --> 00:39:21.068
-[Eric] No. You're going down.
-[instructor] Up. Up you go.


00:39:21.151 --> 00:39:22.810
-I think you should go up.
-No, it's okay. It's fine.


00:39:22.893 --> 00:39:23.949
This is good right here.


00:39:24.085 --> 00:39:25.592
You're just lying on the floor.


00:39:26.161 --> 00:39:27.689
Taking a little nappy-poo.


00:39:27.825 --> 00:39:29.564
It's not a nappy-poo,
it's tango.


00:39:29.699 --> 00:39:32.125
Oh, no. I'm just thinking that
maybe tango isn't our dance.


00:39:32.260 --> 00:39:35.761
-Um, anything else?
-Beth, what else is sexy?


00:39:36.230 --> 00:39:37.863
Come on. Let's keep
our head in the game.


00:39:37.998 --> 00:39:40.341
-Whoo!
-Game point, suckers.


00:39:42.704 --> 00:39:44.477
[distorted breathing]


00:39:52.649 --> 00:39:54.780
-[screams]
-Drop in!


00:39:54.915 --> 00:39:56.685
-[shrieks]
-[grunts]


00:39:56.821 --> 00:39:58.192
Serena Williams,
she's got nothing


00:39:58.328 --> 00:39:59.774
on the sounds these
ladies are making.


00:39:59.857 --> 00:40:02.394
The body-thumping
beat of hip-hop.


00:40:02.530 --> 00:40:04.656
-Like that? Yep.
-Bop, bop, bop. Yes.


00:40:04.792 --> 00:40:05.992
A hop and a hip-hop.


00:40:06.128 --> 00:40:08.329
I've never seen this
kind of hip-hop.


00:40:08.464 --> 00:40:10.529
[Tess shrieking]


00:40:11.331 --> 00:40:12.719
-She's on the ground.
-How is she doing that?


00:40:12.802 --> 00:40:14.067
[opponent] That's a new move.


00:40:14.203 --> 00:40:16.476
That's defensive offense.
Defensive offense!


00:40:17.111 --> 00:40:18.247
Woman, get up!


00:40:20.777 --> 00:40:22.074
[opponent, distorted] Oh, no!


00:40:22.209 --> 00:40:23.917
-That was close!
-Wow! Did you see that?


00:40:24.052 --> 00:40:25.353
Did you see that?


00:40:27.257 --> 00:40:28.417
-Did we win?
-[crowd cheering]


00:40:28.517 --> 00:40:30.391
Yes! Yes!


00:40:32.696 --> 00:40:33.888
We won!


00:40:34.023 --> 00:40:35.139
[opponent] I believe
that was illegal


00:40:35.222 --> 00:40:36.248
and I'd like to
roll back the tapes


00:40:36.331 --> 00:40:37.491
and watch that one more time.


00:40:37.594 --> 00:40:38.928
Take that, boomers!


00:40:39.063 --> 00:40:40.450
-Okay. You know what, no.
-Okay, first of all...


00:40:40.533 --> 00:40:41.895
-Hold me back.
-You stay back.


00:40:42.031 --> 00:40:43.571
-We are not boomers.
-We're Gen X!


00:40:43.707 --> 00:40:46.768
-We are elder millennials.
-Some of the last millennials.


00:40:46.904 --> 00:40:48.468
-The finale.
-[Eric] The finale.


00:40:48.903 --> 00:40:51.473
And five, six, seven, eight.


00:40:51.609 --> 00:40:54.008
Go! And slide. That's it.


00:40:54.144 --> 00:40:56.784
[♪ "(I've Had) The Time
of My Life" playing]


00:40:56.920 --> 00:40:58.347
[Beth] Get it.


00:40:58.482 --> 00:40:59.688
To the side. Whoo!


00:40:59.823 --> 00:41:01.521
Get it. Yes!


00:41:02.390 --> 00:41:04.359
-Ow!
-[instructor grunts]


00:41:12.200 --> 00:41:14.067
[instructor] And Anna.


00:41:14.203 --> 00:41:15.395
-Run, girl.
-Run!


00:41:15.530 --> 00:41:16.732
Anna.


00:41:16.868 --> 00:41:18.172
-Come on, let's go.
-[Beth] Run!


00:41:18.307 --> 00:41:21.277
-Get it. Run. Run.
-Run.


00:41:22.746 --> 00:41:24.203
Anna.


00:41:25.549 --> 00:41:27.509
[Harper] Mom, we're supposed
to know where to go.


00:41:27.645 --> 00:41:28.977
[Lily] Act natural, honey.


00:41:29.113 --> 00:41:31.353
-Detention's that way.
-Can you tell... Okay.


00:41:39.991 --> 00:41:41.929
[Harper] I have an
immigration interview,


00:41:42.064 --> 00:41:43.699
a rehearsal lunch,


00:41:43.834 --> 00:41:47.793
Ella's big show, my wedding,
and I am stuck in detention!


00:41:47.929 --> 00:41:49.295
Well, I'm stuck here too.


00:41:49.430 --> 00:41:52.875
And it's the championships
for the entire Westside.


00:41:53.411 --> 00:41:56.710
Well, well, well.
Look who showed up.


00:41:57.280 --> 00:42:00.649
Lily Reyes and Harper Coleman.


00:42:01.185 --> 00:42:03.275
How have you not retired yet?


00:42:03.411 --> 00:42:06.716
The school had our
pension invested in crypto


00:42:07.085 --> 00:42:08.965
but since I'm not supposed
to complain about it,


00:42:09.086 --> 00:42:11.819
per my lawyer, it's
neither here nor there.


00:42:12.188 --> 00:42:14.788
So let's surrender
our devices Let's go.


00:42:15.357 --> 00:42:18.894
-Mr. Bates... Come on.
-We just got our phones back.


00:42:19.029 --> 00:42:21.430
-That's right. We love school.
-Here.


00:42:21.799 --> 00:42:23.036
[Mr. Bates] Thank you, Simon.


00:42:23.838 --> 00:42:27.670
And now it's time to prepare
for the most boring task


00:42:27.806 --> 00:42:29.902
you could ever possibly imagine.


00:42:30.038 --> 00:42:34.044
Sit there, read or think only.


00:42:34.413 --> 00:42:36.847
No screens, books.


00:42:37.414 --> 00:42:38.346
[groans]


00:42:38.481 --> 00:42:39.515
Wait.


00:42:40.051 --> 00:42:43.148
Does he mean hours of
uninterrupted peace?


00:42:43.283 --> 00:42:45.818
Wipe that look of
bliss off your face.


00:42:45.954 --> 00:42:47.790
Get over yourself, Elton.


00:42:47.926 --> 00:42:49.524
This is high school, not prison.


00:42:49.660 --> 00:42:51.131
Yeah, it's not a prison.


00:42:51.267 --> 00:42:52.994
Which, FYI, research shows


00:42:53.129 --> 00:42:54.936
is ineffective at
preventing recidivism.


00:42:55.071 --> 00:42:56.405
Yeah, "resisism".


00:42:56.540 --> 00:42:58.300
[Lily] You know, giving
back to the community


00:42:58.400 --> 00:43:01.300
is a lot more effective
than trapping people inside.


00:43:02.571 --> 00:43:03.808
Oh!


00:43:04.708 --> 00:43:06.448
You wanna go outside?


00:43:07.346 --> 00:43:08.617
Let us out.


00:43:08.752 --> 00:43:10.499
-[students] Yeah, let us out.
-[Harper] Let us out.


00:43:10.582 --> 00:43:12.683
Let us out. Let us out.


00:43:12.818 --> 00:43:16.686
-Let us out. Let us out.
-Outside.


00:43:17.088 --> 00:43:19.652
-Move it! Let's pick it up!
-[horn honking]


00:43:19.787 --> 00:43:20.954
Out of the way!


00:43:21.089 --> 00:43:23.096
We need to find Madame Jen, now.


00:43:23.232 --> 00:43:24.724
We need our phones.


00:43:25.260 --> 00:43:28.030
Come on, Reyes! You
run like my grandma.


00:43:28.865 --> 00:43:29.997
-Pick it up.
-Rude!


00:43:30.133 --> 00:43:32.441
Pick up the pace or
you'll pick up trash.


00:43:32.576 --> 00:43:34.102
[venue assistant]
<i>It's in two days.</i>


00:43:34.238 --> 00:43:35.796
Yeah, I know. I don't
care about the deposit.


00:43:35.879 --> 00:43:37.555
-<i> And the officiant?</i>
-That includes the officiant?


00:43:37.638 --> 00:43:39.092
-Cancel that, too. Thank you.
-[line disconnects]


00:43:39.175 --> 00:43:40.397
[Siri] <i>Call from
Jett. Answer it?</i>


00:43:40.480 --> 00:43:41.808
Is this for real? Yes.


00:43:41.944 --> 00:43:43.410
[Jett] <i>Where are you?</i>


00:43:43.545 --> 00:43:44.866
<i>The editor from</i>
Rolling Stone<i> is here.</i>


00:43:44.949 --> 00:43:46.455
<i>-Come on! Hurry up!</i>
-Oh, no.


00:43:46.590 --> 00:43:48.917
[editor] Remember,
it's the<i> Hungry Tour.</i>


00:43:49.053 --> 00:43:50.982
Trevor's allergic
to strawberries.


00:43:51.118 --> 00:43:52.527
[editor] Look sweet, Ella.


00:43:53.696 --> 00:43:55.828
-Ella's having a meltdown.
-Morning, Anna.


00:43:55.964 --> 00:43:59.167
Hello, my staff of people
that I see all the time.


00:43:59.303 --> 00:44:01.129
Can you sign off on the dress?


00:44:01.830 --> 00:44:02.764
Here's your juice.


00:44:02.899 --> 00:44:04.039
-Oh, thank you.
-Mm-hmm.


00:44:04.575 --> 00:44:06.904
All right, so she's
over here by this...


00:44:07.739 --> 00:44:09.038
-Girl, what?
-Ugh.


00:44:09.407 --> 00:44:11.942
-Why would you give me that?
-You yell at me if I don't.


00:44:12.077 --> 00:44:15.845
Anna. Jean shorts, rash
guard. Laundry day?


00:44:16.348 --> 00:44:19.912
[sighs] Let's talk about the
headline for the article.


00:44:20.047 --> 00:44:21.589
"It's giving It-Girl.


00:44:21.724 --> 00:44:24.686
Pop star queen Ella
slays down the house."


00:44:24.822 --> 00:44:26.522
-Wait, what?
-Or,


00:44:26.658 --> 00:44:28.122
"We're gagging, besties.


00:44:28.258 --> 00:44:30.625
Ella's new album
just hits different."


00:44:30.760 --> 00:44:32.194
No, no. Just stop.


00:44:32.330 --> 00:44:34.727
What deeply out-of-touch old
person came up with those?


00:44:35.130 --> 00:44:37.664
-You did.
-I did? Wow.


00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:39.100
Thanks, puss.


00:44:39.236 --> 00:44:40.754
Okay, I really need
you to focus on Ella...


00:44:40.837 --> 00:44:42.874
-Okay.
-[Ella sobbing]


00:44:46.545 --> 00:44:47.582
Do something.


00:44:49.612 --> 00:44:50.681
Ella?


00:44:51.317 --> 00:44:54.556
[Ella] Trevor unfollowed me.
And you know what that means?


00:44:55.420 --> 00:44:56.586
No.


00:44:56.721 --> 00:45:00.056
What it means is that


00:45:00.191 --> 00:45:03.492
the whole world knows
that he dumped me.


00:45:03.627 --> 00:45:05.531
It's everywhere!


00:45:06.100 --> 00:45:09.629
Okay. I am your manager,
so I'm gonna manage this.


00:45:09.764 --> 00:45:10.934
Okay.


00:45:11.070 --> 00:45:13.005
[Tess] Ryan, I really
do need to dash.


00:45:13.140 --> 00:45:15.273
But they said the photographer
is back in 5 minutes.


00:45:15.409 --> 00:45:16.636
Photographer?


00:45:16.771 --> 00:45:17.872
Yeah.


00:45:18.007 --> 00:45:19.306
For your new passport photo.


00:45:19.441 --> 00:45:20.859
The one you need for
the international part


00:45:20.942 --> 00:45:22.080
of your book tour?


00:45:22.216 --> 00:45:23.443
Oh, yes.


00:45:23.578 --> 00:45:27.414
I remember every detail
that you told me about me.


00:45:27.549 --> 00:45:31.153
Yeah. I got prescriptions,
you got the essentials.


00:45:32.557 --> 00:45:33.826
Essentials?


00:45:38.265 --> 00:45:39.568
Yes.


00:45:46.167 --> 00:45:48.203
Do I need all these things?


00:45:56.846 --> 00:45:59.016
I need that. Yes.


00:46:00.224 --> 00:46:02.283
Where does this go?


00:46:03.225 --> 00:46:04.417
[retches]


00:46:08.991 --> 00:46:12.297
What? Adult nappies?


00:46:12.432 --> 00:46:14.394
That is so lazy.


00:46:15.869 --> 00:46:18.035
-Oh, hey.
-Yes. Right here.


00:46:20.905 --> 00:46:22.136
-Fixodent?
-Yes.


00:46:22.272 --> 00:46:24.203
Isn't that toothpaste
for old people?


00:46:24.605 --> 00:46:27.374
No. This is for when
you lose your teeth.


00:46:31.750 --> 00:46:33.545
I'm gonna lose my teeth?


00:46:34.750 --> 00:46:35.686
No!


00:46:35.821 --> 00:46:37.253
[Mr. Bates] Okay, slowpokes.


00:46:37.388 --> 00:46:40.891
I want every blue spirulina
smoothie spill gone.


00:46:41.026 --> 00:46:42.992
I want every chia seed scraped.


00:46:43.128 --> 00:46:44.994
Every chewed piece
of organic gum


00:46:45.130 --> 00:46:46.926
on the bottoms of
these seats gone!


00:46:47.061 --> 00:46:48.061
Way to go, Harper.


00:46:48.164 --> 00:46:49.348
Use your nails if you have to.


00:46:49.431 --> 00:46:52.534
What? No, this was Lily's fault.


00:46:52.669 --> 00:46:53.906
Elton.


00:46:55.001 --> 00:46:56.471
Yeah?


00:46:56.606 --> 00:46:59.274
I understand that you feel
the need to prove a point


00:46:59.409 --> 00:47:02.246
because I publicly
undermined your authority.


00:47:02.382 --> 00:47:03.410
Oh!


00:47:04.849 --> 00:47:06.785
Do you understand me?


00:47:06.920 --> 00:47:08.132
This isn't restorative justice.


00:47:08.215 --> 00:47:09.515
I mean, if anything,


00:47:09.650 --> 00:47:12.024
you're making these kids
want to act out more.


00:47:12.160 --> 00:47:14.856
How does Lily always manage
to make things worse?


00:47:14.991 --> 00:47:16.358
It's a unique talent.


00:47:16.493 --> 00:47:18.249
I have connections on
the school board, Elton.


00:47:18.332 --> 00:47:21.627
Well, you're a stupid kid
and you have no connections,


00:47:21.762 --> 00:47:25.967
but you have earned,
along with everybody here,


00:47:26.103 --> 00:47:27.704
three more weeks of detention.


00:47:27.840 --> 00:47:30.005
-Oh, my...
-Lily!


00:47:30.141 --> 00:47:32.241
-Bro!
-Your royal highness.


00:47:33.076 --> 00:47:34.546
-Come on!
-My God!


00:47:34.681 --> 00:47:36.047
That was uncalled for.


00:47:36.182 --> 00:47:40.480
Let's all take a deep,
centering breath.


00:47:42.122 --> 00:47:43.369
[detention student]
Meditate on this!


00:47:43.452 --> 00:47:44.852
Take a deep breath
of this trash.


00:47:44.987 --> 00:47:46.222
[Tess] You ready?


00:47:46.891 --> 00:47:48.125
[photographer] Stunning.


00:47:48.923 --> 00:47:50.056
Wow.


00:47:50.191 --> 00:47:51.425
[muffled] Good, right?


00:47:53.002 --> 00:47:55.262
I think you're having
an allergic reaction.


00:47:55.397 --> 00:47:58.102
No, no, no, no.
It's lip plumper.


00:47:58.705 --> 00:47:59.705
I'm gonna get some ice.


00:47:59.840 --> 00:48:01.105
Okay, give me the ring light.


00:48:01.240 --> 00:48:03.239
And every bottle of
Benadryl I can find.


00:48:03.374 --> 00:48:05.510
[Tess, muffled] It's
lip plumper. No, Ryan.


00:48:05.646 --> 00:48:07.446
I don't have allergies.


00:48:07.582 --> 00:48:08.715
Oh. Okay, whatever.


00:48:08.851 --> 00:48:10.147
Do you have another ring light?


00:48:10.282 --> 00:48:11.629
-Like, a big ring light?
-[photographer] Sure.


00:48:11.712 --> 00:48:13.546
-And another thing. Can you...
-Yeah, okay.


00:48:13.681 --> 00:48:16.322
You hold the ring light.
I'll pose. Okay, ready?


00:48:16.457 --> 00:48:17.484
I got it.


00:48:21.629 --> 00:48:23.160
Let me look. Hold on.


00:48:24.161 --> 00:48:27.429
Oh, no. Just 10, maybe 15 more.


00:48:27.564 --> 00:48:30.871
I'll give you looks, okay?
All right, here I go.


00:48:33.405 --> 00:48:36.136
[Tess] "Dear Sir, must
cancel the wedding venue


00:48:36.272 --> 00:48:37.744
because the bride is horrible,


00:48:37.880 --> 00:48:39.972
as my daughter
always suspected."


00:48:40.107 --> 00:48:42.282
Oh! Who's Laura?


00:48:42.418 --> 00:48:43.944
Hello, hello.


00:48:44.079 --> 00:48:46.135
[Laura] <i>Hey, hon. I need your
approval on the author photo.</i>


00:48:46.218 --> 00:48:48.284
-Okay.
-<i> Texting it over now.</i>


00:48:49.052 --> 00:48:51.787
[Tess] Oh, no. No, no.


00:48:51.923 --> 00:48:53.394
That one's rubbish.


00:48:53.529 --> 00:48:55.223
I just took a new one.


00:48:55.359 --> 00:48:57.194
-I'm sending now.
-<i> Thanks.</i>


00:48:57.329 --> 00:49:01.528
Oh, look. Her phone has
the giant letter virus.


00:49:03.338 --> 00:49:04.632
Oh!


00:49:04.768 --> 00:49:07.841
Ryan. Is it possible for you
to drop me at Anna's work?


00:49:07.977 --> 00:49:09.290
[announcer] <i>Hey,
you Trevorheads.</i>


00:49:09.373 --> 00:49:10.733
<i>That was your boy,
Trevor Travis,</i>


00:49:10.844 --> 00:49:12.074
<i>with his brand-new song,</i>


00:49:12.209 --> 00:49:13.509
<i>"Better than the Last One."</i>


00:49:14.412 --> 00:49:16.208
My mom's biggest client
is having a meltdown.


00:49:16.344 --> 00:49:17.718
-Jett!
-I'm working!


00:49:17.854 --> 00:49:19.986
Trevor, her
boyfriend, dumped her.


00:49:21.358 --> 00:49:22.358
Trevor Travis?


00:49:22.685 --> 00:49:25.956
♪ <i>She's so much better Better</i> ♪


00:49:26.091 --> 00:49:27.459
♪ <i>Better than the</i> ♪


00:49:27.828 --> 00:49:30.295
♪ <i>Last one</i> ♪


00:49:30.431 --> 00:49:31.531
[gasps]


00:49:32.033 --> 00:49:34.867
And they just got
matching tattoos.


00:49:35.002 --> 00:49:39.205
That is literally
the worst thing


00:49:39.341 --> 00:49:42.709
I have ever heard happening
to anyone ever, full stop.


00:49:42.844 --> 00:49:44.671
-Thank you.
-Of course.


00:49:45.207 --> 00:49:46.714
Anna's getting married,


00:49:46.850 --> 00:49:47.778
so she doesn't
get what it's like


00:49:47.914 --> 00:49:49.211
to have your heart broken.


00:49:49.347 --> 00:49:51.752
I know. When I was
your age, my mom...


00:49:51.888 --> 00:49:54.449
I mean, I had this
boyfriend, Jake,


00:49:54.585 --> 00:49:57.019
and all my friends say
he was my first love.


00:49:57.155 --> 00:49:59.159
Is that who your song's about?


00:49:59.562 --> 00:50:01.126
What song? My song?


00:50:07.434 --> 00:50:10.003
[Anna, through speakers]
♪ <i>See you in my dreams</i> ♪


00:50:11.406 --> 00:50:14.968
♪ <i>Whenever you go I
tear at the seams</i> ♪


00:50:15.104 --> 00:50:16.038
I wrote that?


00:50:16.173 --> 00:50:19.045
[chuckles] It's really good.


00:50:19.912 --> 00:50:22.416
This is a great song.


00:50:22.552 --> 00:50:24.716
You're really good.


00:50:25.152 --> 00:50:27.119
I don't get why
you quit playing.


00:50:28.525 --> 00:50:30.047
Because I had a kid


00:50:30.183 --> 00:50:33.856
who I probably resent since
I'm writing songs in secret.


00:50:33.992 --> 00:50:35.831
So, you miss performing?


00:50:37.633 --> 00:50:39.964
I mean, yeah, probably.


00:50:40.399 --> 00:50:42.904
I'm finding out a lot
about myself today.


00:50:44.003 --> 00:50:45.498
-[music stops]
-[sighs]


00:50:45.634 --> 00:50:49.140
Anna, your song is
the only song I loved


00:50:49.275 --> 00:50:51.040
out of everything
that we got sent.


00:50:51.175 --> 00:50:52.914
I know you already said no,


00:50:53.049 --> 00:50:57.016
but can I please sing it
at the Wiltern tomorrow?


00:50:57.151 --> 00:50:59.446
I mean, it's your
concert, your tour.


00:50:59.582 --> 00:51:01.813
You should sing
whatever song you want.


00:51:02.558 --> 00:51:03.991
Okay. Yeah, just...


00:51:04.126 --> 00:51:06.990
I feel like between
managers and stylists


00:51:07.125 --> 00:51:09.229
and execs and label people,


00:51:09.365 --> 00:51:13.168
I feel like I never get a
say in anything that goes on.


00:51:13.303 --> 00:51:14.303
Right?


00:51:14.565 --> 00:51:18.236
Right, because old
people never listen.


00:51:19.039 --> 00:51:21.443
I mean, people like you think...


00:51:21.578 --> 00:51:22.734
I think people like me


00:51:22.870 --> 00:51:24.127
think people like
you don't know any...


00:51:24.210 --> 00:51:26.341
-You know what I mean.
-Yeah.


00:51:26.477 --> 00:51:28.613
I have control over my own life.


00:51:29.349 --> 00:51:31.380
Absolute control.
Photoshoot's back on.


00:51:31.515 --> 00:51:33.586
Photoshoot is back
on, grasshoppers.


00:51:33.721 --> 00:51:35.018
Chop, chop, chop.


00:51:35.154 --> 00:51:37.759
Let's make some fierce photos


00:51:37.895 --> 00:51:40.190
of this fierce girl right here.


00:51:40.325 --> 00:51:42.025
Bruh, having a job
is really hard.


00:51:42.161 --> 00:51:44.032
-Wait.
-What? "Wait" what?


00:51:44.167 --> 00:51:48.236
If your mum wrote that
song about that Jake...


00:51:48.371 --> 00:51:49.698
Yeah.


00:51:49.834 --> 00:51:51.453
...that's how we can get our
parents to split up forever.


00:51:51.536 --> 00:51:54.938
So if she is with him,
she can't marry my dad.


00:51:55.074 --> 00:51:56.439
Well, how do we find him?


00:51:58.279 --> 00:52:00.880
[Tess] It's like a
database of old people.


00:52:01.282 --> 00:52:03.684
-Jake. Yes.
-That's him from the photo.


00:52:03.820 --> 00:52:05.415
[Tess] Wait, wait, wait, look.


00:52:06.313 --> 00:52:07.250
[Tess] Okay.


00:52:07.386 --> 00:52:09.089
And he owns the Record Parlour.


00:52:09.224 --> 00:52:12.189
[Tess] He has liked
all your mum's posts.


00:52:12.325 --> 00:52:15.024
He is proper obsessed with her.


00:52:15.160 --> 00:52:17.189
Single. Okay, let's do it.


00:52:17.324 --> 00:52:18.895
Let's do it.


00:52:19.365 --> 00:52:21.629
But first, your
mum must look fit


00:52:21.764 --> 00:52:23.835
if she's gonna run into
the love of her life.


00:52:23.971 --> 00:52:25.403
And I need to change, too.


00:52:25.538 --> 00:52:29.174
Ella's stylist has pulled
the most gorgeous garms


00:52:29.309 --> 00:52:30.601
I've ever seen in
my entire life.


00:52:30.737 --> 00:52:31.945
[Ella] Do we love this for me?


00:52:32.081 --> 00:52:33.296
Girl, the label
loves this for you.


00:52:33.379 --> 00:52:34.782
-Can we just put it on your...
-No.


00:52:34.917 --> 00:52:36.037
-Maybe on your shoulder?
-No.


00:52:36.147 --> 00:52:37.747
Rest it on your head?


00:52:37.883 --> 00:52:40.152
[Tess] <i>Please, can we just
put our differences aside</i>


00:52:40.287 --> 00:52:42.923
so that I can live
my dream? Please.


00:52:43.059 --> 00:52:44.891
This is only
because of the plan.


00:52:45.026 --> 00:52:46.819
-Oh, thank you.
-You're welcome.


00:52:48.262 --> 00:52:50.695
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.


00:52:51.598 --> 00:52:54.365
[♪ "Super Graphic Ultra
Modern Girl" playing]


00:53:01.105 --> 00:53:02.673
It's not very me.


00:53:03.175 --> 00:53:05.575
Harper. This is so exciting.


00:53:05.710 --> 00:53:07.979
So, posing for the camera,
it's very different.


00:53:08.115 --> 00:53:09.982
Find a shape and then hold it.


00:53:10.117 --> 00:53:11.877
-Yeah. Okay.
-Good luck.


00:53:14.748 --> 00:53:16.486
-Where did the fruit go?
-I'm s...


00:53:21.895 --> 00:53:23.195
Oh, this is cool.


00:53:23.331 --> 00:53:25.033
-Oh, that is chic.
-It's recycled I think.


00:53:25.966 --> 00:53:26.798
'Cause I'm a pop star.


00:53:26.934 --> 00:53:28.102
-Pop out.
-Yeah.


00:53:28.570 --> 00:53:29.570
Pop.


00:53:30.034 --> 00:53:31.270
No! No! No! No!


00:53:32.641 --> 00:53:34.438
No, no, no.


00:53:34.907 --> 00:53:36.077
[in unison] Oh.


00:53:45.046 --> 00:53:47.055
[Ella] <i>Tess, your
styling is so on point.</i>


00:53:47.190 --> 00:53:49.521
You two are the coolest
adults I have ever met.


00:53:49.657 --> 00:53:50.657
Thanks.


00:53:50.784 --> 00:53:51.993
-Bye.
-[Tess] Thank you.


00:53:52.128 --> 00:53:53.820
-My mom does have a cool job.
-Yes.


00:53:57.430 --> 00:53:58.929
Think she's our new best friend?


00:53:59.065 --> 00:54:01.698
I think so. I think so.


00:54:02.101 --> 00:54:03.461
Do you guys need a ride?


00:54:03.897 --> 00:54:05.902
-Oh, yes. Totally. Yes.
-OMG, yes.


00:54:06.037 --> 00:54:07.600
[PA chimes]


00:54:07.735 --> 00:54:09.310
[Waldman] <i>Attention, students.</i>


00:54:09.446 --> 00:54:10.921
<i>You'll be happy to know
that my anaphylactic shock</i>


00:54:11.004 --> 00:54:13.114
<i>-has subsided.</i>
-[retches]


00:54:14.474 --> 00:54:15.474
[retches]


00:54:15.880 --> 00:54:18.779
-[Waldman] <i>Yes. I didn't die.</i>
-[Mr. Bates snoring]


00:54:19.886 --> 00:54:21.078
Thank you.


00:54:21.514 --> 00:54:22.589
[retches]


00:54:22.724 --> 00:54:24.115
[PA chimes]


00:54:24.250 --> 00:54:26.051
[Waldman] <i>And I hope
those who were involved</i>


00:54:26.186 --> 00:54:28.921
<i>in that food fight
are loving detention.</i>


00:54:34.560 --> 00:54:36.236
[fans cheering]


00:54:39.674 --> 00:54:40.900
Oh, no.


00:54:42.143 --> 00:54:44.443
They've gone completely rogue.


00:54:44.845 --> 00:54:45.947
[Tess] Whoo!


00:54:46.082 --> 00:54:48.674
-Yeah!
-[Tess] <i>This is so cool!</i>


00:54:48.809 --> 00:54:50.380
[Lily] What are we wearing?


00:54:50.515 --> 00:54:52.544
They're on a joyride with Ella.


00:54:52.679 --> 00:54:54.186
We'll never find them.


00:54:54.322 --> 00:54:58.357
No, but we can find Madame Jen.


00:55:02.362 --> 00:55:04.429
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?


00:55:05.492 --> 00:55:06.530
Oh, yeah.


00:55:07.894 --> 00:55:09.803
[♪ "Spice Up Your Life" plays]


00:55:09.938 --> 00:55:11.455
-♪<i> Every boy and every girl</i> ♪
-♪<i> Spice up your life</i> ♪


00:55:11.538 --> 00:55:13.336
[Lily] Madame Jen said
she lost her table


00:55:13.471 --> 00:55:15.234
at the Larchmont Farmers Market,


00:55:15.369 --> 00:55:17.495
but now she can be seen at the
Starbucks across the street


00:55:17.578 --> 00:55:20.808
from the Larchmont Village
wine and cheese shop.


00:55:23.153 --> 00:55:24.552
Look, I know we
don't have time...


00:55:24.687 --> 00:55:25.945
But we are here.


00:55:26.080 --> 00:55:28.223
And my metabolism is
the speed of sound.


00:55:28.358 --> 00:55:30.915
-♪<i> Spice up your life</i> ♪
-[vocalizing]


00:55:31.050 --> 00:55:32.892
[Harper] I got
extra whipped cream!


00:55:33.027 --> 00:55:35.186
[Lily] My knees work!


00:55:35.322 --> 00:55:37.961
I haven't had real dairy
since Bush was president.


00:55:38.096 --> 00:55:39.360
Curly fries!


00:55:39.495 --> 00:55:40.928
[Harper] Flexibility!


00:55:41.063 --> 00:55:42.836
♪ <i>If ya know That
you feel fine</i> ♪


00:55:42.972 --> 00:55:44.566
-Mmm.
-[laughs]


00:55:44.702 --> 00:55:47.033
We really need to
find Madame Jen.


00:55:47.168 --> 00:55:50.911
Yes, but they have onion
rings on their burgers.


00:55:51.347 --> 00:55:54.044
I haven't digested
like this in decades!


00:55:54.180 --> 00:55:56.074
I'm still not full!


00:55:56.685 --> 00:55:57.845
Sugar.


00:55:58.446 --> 00:55:59.779
Remember sugar?


00:55:59.915 --> 00:56:01.680
But after this,
back to the mission.


00:56:01.816 --> 00:56:03.314
Mmm. It has my full attention.


00:56:03.450 --> 00:56:07.395
All you have to do is go in
there and flirt with Jake,


00:56:07.531 --> 00:56:10.098
and remind him why he fancied
you when you were young.


00:56:10.233 --> 00:56:11.657
Wait, I wasn't me
when I was young.


00:56:11.793 --> 00:56:13.358
And I don't know how to flirt.


00:56:13.493 --> 00:56:15.487
And I definitely don't know
how to flirt as an old person.


00:56:15.570 --> 00:56:18.531
What do they do, talk
about transitional lenses?


00:56:18.667 --> 00:56:20.868
Home repairs? John Mayer?


00:56:21.003 --> 00:56:22.700
-I... I don't know.
-Oh! I have an idea.


00:56:22.836 --> 00:56:24.745
We both wear our AirPods.


00:56:24.881 --> 00:56:26.004
That way you can help me


00:56:26.139 --> 00:56:27.398
because you have a
French boyfriend.


00:56:27.481 --> 00:56:29.382
So you definitely
know how to flirt.


00:56:30.545 --> 00:56:33.210
Yeah... Defo. Yes.


00:56:33.346 --> 00:56:35.226
I'm gonna go in, and then
I'll give you the word


00:56:35.349 --> 00:56:37.757
when to come in and make
your sexy grand entrance.


00:56:38.527 --> 00:56:40.521
What sexy grand entrance?
What do you mean?


00:56:40.656 --> 00:56:41.673
[Tess] You have to be sexy.


00:56:41.756 --> 00:56:42.956
-How?
-[Tess] Like...


00:56:44.425 --> 00:56:45.464
Sexy.


00:56:46.199 --> 00:56:47.393
I'm not doing that.


00:56:47.528 --> 00:56:49.831
[engine roaring]


00:56:54.109 --> 00:56:56.707
-[engine revs]
-Oh.


00:56:57.343 --> 00:56:59.072
♪ <i>Oh, my God</i> ♪


00:56:59.207 --> 00:57:01.849
♪ <i>Take me back The
way that I was</i> ♪


00:57:01.985 --> 00:57:04.816
♪ <i>Oh, my God</i> ♪


00:57:04.952 --> 00:57:07.519
♪ <i>You know I only tried
to Play your games</i> ♪


00:57:07.655 --> 00:57:10.285
♪ <i>So you cannot Forget my name</i> ♪


00:57:10.420 --> 00:57:15.093
♪ <i>You and I are not the same
You always had it easy</i> ♪


00:57:15.229 --> 00:57:17.057
♪ <i>Oh, my God</i> ♪


00:57:17.192 --> 00:57:20.199
♪ <i>Take me back The
way that I was</i> ♪


00:57:20.334 --> 00:57:22.802
♪ <i>The way that I was</i> ♪


00:57:22.937 --> 00:57:24.437
[chuckles]


00:57:27.370 --> 00:57:28.408
[Jake] Hey!


00:57:31.139 --> 00:57:33.646
-This is a different look.
-Yeah. Uh-huh.


00:57:33.782 --> 00:57:36.207
It's awesome. I didn't know
you were coming by today.


00:57:36.342 --> 00:57:38.214
-I got the stuff in the back.
-What stuff?


00:57:38.349 --> 00:57:39.349
What do you mean?


00:57:39.687 --> 00:57:41.856
[Tess] <i>That's him.
That's her bloke.</i>


00:57:41.991 --> 00:57:43.390
<i>What's happening?</i>


00:57:44.192 --> 00:57:45.855
He's going to get me stuff.


00:57:45.991 --> 00:57:48.822
What is your mother doing
behind my father's back?


00:57:48.957 --> 00:57:51.693
-[shushes]
-No. Hey, hey, hey!


00:57:51.828 --> 00:57:53.324
-Do not shush me. Okay?
-Get down.


00:57:53.459 --> 00:57:55.367
-He can't hear me.
-Get down. I'm ignoring you.


00:57:55.502 --> 00:57:57.371
Hey, thanks again
for doing this.


00:57:57.506 --> 00:58:01.770
What exactly are we
doing here? [chuckles]


00:58:01.906 --> 00:58:03.643
Signing the merch for
the charity auction.


00:58:03.779 --> 00:58:05.011
Oh.


00:58:05.147 --> 00:58:07.041
-Right.
-Here you go.


00:58:07.543 --> 00:58:10.483
Right. The merch.


00:58:11.612 --> 00:58:12.612
[Tess] Oh!


00:58:16.090 --> 00:58:17.557
I have a question.


00:58:18.226 --> 00:58:19.617
Do you ever think about me?


00:58:19.752 --> 00:58:21.260
About us?


00:58:21.729 --> 00:58:24.097
I'm not sure there's a right
answer to this question.


00:58:24.232 --> 00:58:30.338
I mean, do you ever miss us?


00:58:32.034 --> 00:58:34.166
You're getting
married this weekend.


00:58:34.844 --> 00:58:38.071
Unless I'm not.


00:58:38.907 --> 00:58:40.438
["...Baby One More Time" plays]


00:58:40.573 --> 00:58:42.543
[Tess] <i>Okay, very good.
Now, do something cheeky.</i>


00:58:42.678 --> 00:58:44.319
Like, flip your hair.


00:58:45.283 --> 00:58:46.520
<i>Good.</i>


00:58:46.656 --> 00:58:49.115
<i>Ooh, good. Big, big,
big moves. Big moves.</i>


00:58:49.251 --> 00:58:51.649
<i>One more. Shake
your head. Shake it.</i>


00:58:52.418 --> 00:58:54.753
<i>More. Like, all the way around.</i>


00:58:54.889 --> 00:58:56.155
<i>There you go. Shake it.</i>


00:58:57.098 --> 00:58:58.498
<i>Excellent.</i>


00:58:58.634 --> 00:59:01.669
<i>Okay, um, wink at him.
Try winking. Wink.</i>


00:59:01.804 --> 00:59:02.860
Wink.


00:59:02.996 --> 00:59:05.234
<i>Wink. One eye. One eye.</i>


00:59:05.369 --> 00:59:06.497
Now do both.


00:59:06.999 --> 00:59:09.905
<i>Wink. Okay, good.</i>


00:59:12.182 --> 00:59:14.276
Okay. Um, that's not working.


00:59:14.411 --> 00:59:15.841
Um... Uh... Oh!


00:59:15.977 --> 00:59:18.276
Bite your lip. Bite your lip.


00:59:20.149 --> 00:59:22.284
<i>Why is he looking
at you like that?</i>


00:59:22.719 --> 00:59:23.882
[muffled] I'm biting my lip.


00:59:24.285 --> 00:59:26.389
No, not your top
lip. Your bottom lip.


00:59:26.524 --> 00:59:27.995
Bite your bottom lip.


00:59:28.130 --> 00:59:29.958
<i>Like that, pouty.</i>


00:59:30.726 --> 00:59:32.091
I know what this is.


00:59:32.227 --> 00:59:33.915
I've seen this before.
You're having a stroke.


00:59:33.998 --> 00:59:35.322
-Mm-mmm. No, no.
-We need to get you help.


00:59:35.405 --> 00:59:37.096
I just need to go
to the bathroom.


00:59:37.232 --> 00:59:38.624
I just... Yeah. Gotta
go to the bathroom.


00:59:38.707 --> 00:59:40.798
-Uh, it's in the back.
-All right. I'll find it.


00:59:40.933 --> 00:59:42.839
Are you sure? I...


00:59:48.184 --> 00:59:49.510
There's no merch in the...


00:59:50.113 --> 00:59:52.548
I was really bad at
that. So bad at that.


00:59:52.984 --> 00:59:55.115
How do you know your
boyfriend liked you?


00:59:55.617 --> 00:59:56.450
[stammers]


00:59:56.586 --> 00:59:57.586
You just know.


00:59:57.717 --> 00:59:58.651
Huh?


00:59:58.787 --> 01:00:00.459
How? Like, specifically.


01:00:00.594 --> 01:00:02.321
You've dated a
guy. You know this.


01:00:02.456 --> 01:00:05.125
You have experience. Tell
me. Help me out here.


01:00:07.637 --> 01:00:10.165
Harper, I... I don't
have a French boyfriend.


01:00:10.301 --> 01:00:11.329
[gasps]


01:00:12.736 --> 01:00:14.542
My entire dating experience


01:00:14.677 --> 01:00:17.171
is watching 500
hours of<i> Love Island</i>.


01:00:17.306 --> 01:00:19.539
Wait, you're, like, the most
confident person I know.


01:00:19.674 --> 01:00:21.207
It's an act.


01:00:24.744 --> 01:00:26.112
What?


01:00:26.248 --> 01:00:28.048
Well, you're not gonna
tell everyone, are you?


01:00:28.450 --> 01:00:31.419
No. I'm not like that. I
wouldn't do that. [chuckles]


01:00:31.554 --> 01:00:32.854
Okay. Thank you.


01:00:32.990 --> 01:00:34.962
Oh! You're not gonna
hug me, are you?


01:00:35.098 --> 01:00:36.530
No, I was... Just...


01:00:36.665 --> 01:00:38.490
-No, don't do that.
-Okay, it was just...


01:00:38.626 --> 01:00:40.996
All right, look, no, we should
get back out there. Right?


01:00:41.131 --> 01:00:43.561
Because, otherwise,
he'll think I'm pooping.


01:00:43.696 --> 01:00:45.482
-[Lily] There she is!
-I see her. Right by the milk.


01:00:45.565 --> 01:00:48.141
And I see your screenwriting
career taking off.


01:00:48.277 --> 01:00:50.773
If you move over to, um...


01:00:50.908 --> 01:00:53.374
-[barista] Genre?
-Genre, yes.


01:00:53.509 --> 01:00:54.378
Genre.


01:00:54.514 --> 01:00:55.514
[barista] Elevated genre?


01:00:55.643 --> 01:00:56.847
Um...


01:00:57.283 --> 01:00:58.814
No. Sorry.


01:00:58.950 --> 01:01:01.118
-[Harper] You!
-[Madame Jen] Um. Oh.


01:01:01.253 --> 01:01:02.021
Um...


01:01:02.156 --> 01:01:03.089
How can I help?


01:01:03.225 --> 01:01:06.523
Take one wild guess.


01:01:06.659 --> 01:01:08.529
Are you gonna serve me papers?


01:01:09.660 --> 01:01:11.961
We switched bodies.


01:01:12.594 --> 01:01:13.692
Oh!


01:01:13.827 --> 01:01:15.196
Oh, my gosh.


01:01:15.732 --> 01:01:17.362
It actually worked.


01:01:17.963 --> 01:01:19.601
That's amazing.


01:01:19.737 --> 01:01:21.201
It's never worked before.


01:01:21.336 --> 01:01:23.539
Um, would you guys mind
leaving me a review


01:01:23.674 --> 01:01:24.874
or, like, five stars?


01:01:25.009 --> 01:01:26.299
And just saying,
like, "Oh, my gosh!


01:01:26.382 --> 01:01:27.745
Madame Jen was so much fun..."


01:01:27.880 --> 01:01:29.320
Tell us how to switch
back right now.


01:01:29.414 --> 01:01:30.451
Okay. All right.


01:01:30.587 --> 01:01:32.586
Um, I'll consider it
if you sign up for


01:01:32.721 --> 01:01:36.581
my Reiki and financial
management package.


01:01:36.717 --> 01:01:39.894
Tell us how to switch back,
you multi-hyphenate lunatic!


01:01:40.497 --> 01:01:43.460
Oh, my gosh. I am
a multi-hyphenate.


01:01:43.595 --> 01:01:45.027
That absolutely slays.


01:01:45.162 --> 01:01:47.760
I'm supposed to get
married in two days.


01:01:47.895 --> 01:01:49.597
Right, okay. Um...


01:01:50.333 --> 01:01:53.300
All right. Well, you have
to look at the reading.


01:01:53.436 --> 01:01:57.206
-That's the only way.
-We don't know the reading.


01:01:57.875 --> 01:01:59.580
Um, what are you talking about?


01:01:59.715 --> 01:02:01.911
I said the reading
directly to you both,


01:02:02.047 --> 01:02:04.415
multiple times, in a
scary whisper voice.


01:02:04.551 --> 01:02:06.147
Because we weren't there.


01:02:06.848 --> 01:02:07.780
That wasn't...


01:02:07.915 --> 01:02:09.786
Right! Oh, right.


01:02:09.922 --> 01:02:12.184
You weren't you because
you had switched


01:02:12.320 --> 01:02:15.424
with the other women, who are...


01:02:15.559 --> 01:02:16.690
Okay, that's...


01:02:16.826 --> 01:02:18.160
And it makes sense.


01:02:18.295 --> 01:02:22.767
Um, okay. Well... [sighs]
...the reading was,


01:02:22.902 --> 01:02:24.901
"Change the hearts
you know are wrong


01:02:25.036 --> 01:02:27.938
to reach the place
where you belong."


01:02:28.073 --> 01:02:29.793
-Didn't we try that?
-I think we tried that.


01:02:29.909 --> 01:02:32.072
-We tried it.
-Okay, the problem is


01:02:32.208 --> 01:02:34.708
your hearts might
not be the only ones


01:02:34.844 --> 01:02:36.213
that need changing.


01:02:36.348 --> 01:02:37.376
So...


01:02:37.878 --> 01:02:39.712
Mmm. Cute.


01:02:39.847 --> 01:02:40.847
[chuckles]


01:02:40.982 --> 01:02:42.914
Well, our time is up.


01:02:43.450 --> 01:02:45.121
[Harper] Wait,
but... No, no, no.


01:02:45.256 --> 01:02:46.912
There's got to be something
else you can do, right?


01:02:46.995 --> 01:02:49.559
I wish I could help you,
but my shift is starting.


01:02:50.261 --> 01:02:54.299
So, what I can do for
you is get you a cortado,


01:02:54.434 --> 01:02:56.564
an Americano, a...


01:02:56.699 --> 01:02:58.299
[mumbles]


01:02:58.434 --> 01:03:01.800
...and any kind of espresso
or non-espresso drink.


01:03:01.936 --> 01:03:02.869
[phone rings]


01:03:03.004 --> 01:03:04.070
It's your dad! Shoot!


01:03:04.206 --> 01:03:05.906
[Jake] This is all new inventory


01:03:06.041 --> 01:03:07.439
that we need to get sorted.


01:03:08.745 --> 01:03:10.112
Uh, excuse me.


01:03:11.484 --> 01:03:12.785
-Tess?
-Oh!


01:03:16.019 --> 01:03:17.922
What are you doing down there?


01:03:18.919 --> 01:03:20.320
Stretching.


01:03:21.692 --> 01:03:23.895
Ah. Yeah. I...


01:03:24.398 --> 01:03:25.689
Anna didn't...


01:03:25.825 --> 01:03:27.683
She didn't tell me that you
were gonna be here today.


01:03:27.766 --> 01:03:29.032
-Oh!
-What interview?


01:03:29.167 --> 01:03:30.547
I mean, yes, I know
the interview. Now?


01:03:30.630 --> 01:03:33.269
I was just thinking
about you the other day.


01:03:33.405 --> 01:03:34.637
Really?


01:03:35.140 --> 01:03:36.556
I've been meaning to
ask you something.


01:03:36.639 --> 01:03:38.142
Sure.


01:03:38.278 --> 01:03:43.245
And, um, I don't quite know
how to broach the subject.


01:03:43.380 --> 01:03:49.422
But is, um, your husband...
Is he still with us?


01:03:49.958 --> 01:03:53.689
Yeah. I can't believe
it. I mean, he's so old.


01:03:53.824 --> 01:03:56.163
How... How old is he?


01:03:56.299 --> 01:03:58.222
We never talk about it.


01:03:58.358 --> 01:04:00.595
Somewhere between 50 and 100.


01:04:00.730 --> 01:04:02.267
[chuckles]


01:04:02.403 --> 01:04:03.562
[Tess] Really.


01:04:03.697 --> 01:04:07.739
Yeah. Yeah. But... Okay,
let me focus for a second.


01:04:07.874 --> 01:04:10.136
I'm worried about
Anna, all right?


01:04:10.271 --> 01:04:11.636
She's been being weird with me,


01:04:11.771 --> 01:04:14.879
and she keeps asking if
I ever think about her.


01:04:15.015 --> 01:04:17.715
You know, maybe she
is reconsidering.


01:04:17.850 --> 01:04:19.646
-Reconsidering?
-[Tess] Uh-huh.


01:04:19.781 --> 01:04:23.185
Three weeks ago, she told me
how in love she is with Eric.


01:04:23.321 --> 01:04:26.155
Do you know that she
wrote a song about you?


01:04:27.527 --> 01:04:28.861
-No.
-Anna!


01:04:29.891 --> 01:04:31.260
Daughter.


01:04:31.395 --> 01:04:34.494
Why don't you tell Jake
about the song you wrote?


01:04:35.030 --> 01:04:36.463
I wrote a song about us.


01:04:36.599 --> 01:04:38.253
[Tess] You know what, I'll
give you your privacy.


01:04:38.336 --> 01:04:40.365
I'm just gonna go look
for music for old people.


01:04:40.501 --> 01:04:43.243
You know, really
old, like Coldplay.


01:04:43.879 --> 01:04:45.438
It's nice to hear
you're writing again.


01:04:45.573 --> 01:04:47.708
Yeah, can you just
give me a second, bro?


01:04:47.843 --> 01:04:49.376
Just one second.


01:04:50.010 --> 01:04:51.610
Coldplay...


01:04:51.746 --> 01:04:54.015
We need to get to the
immigration interview. Now.


01:04:54.150 --> 01:04:56.089
-Okay, let's go.
-[Anna] Yeah.


01:04:56.458 --> 01:04:57.988
Oh! My legs are so weak,


01:04:58.123 --> 01:05:00.321
my knees are cracking
like walnuts.


01:05:01.527 --> 01:05:02.554
[knees pop]


01:05:04.026 --> 01:05:05.729
[breathing heavily]


01:05:05.864 --> 01:05:07.500
What is happening right now?


01:05:07.969 --> 01:05:10.495
My brain is telling
my body to stand up,


01:05:10.631 --> 01:05:13.367
but it's like shouting
into the abyss.


01:05:14.942 --> 01:05:16.637
See? I just tried
to get up again.


01:05:16.772 --> 01:05:17.841
Okay.


01:05:17.976 --> 01:05:19.541
-Help me. Help me up.
-Okay.


01:05:19.676 --> 01:05:21.226
We have to find a way to get
to the immigration interview.


01:05:21.309 --> 01:05:22.482
-[Tess] Okay.
-[Anna] Yes.


01:05:22.618 --> 01:05:25.084
Wait, I have an idea. Come on.


01:05:25.219 --> 01:05:26.872
[Jake] So, that's why Tess
and I have a special bond.


01:05:26.955 --> 01:05:30.088
Oh, Jake. Hi. Could
we borrow your car?


01:05:30.224 --> 01:05:33.920
Oh, and don't worry, we're
totally of age to drive.


01:05:34.056 --> 01:05:36.962
Anything for you, Dr. C.


01:05:39.334 --> 01:05:40.334
You ready?


01:05:41.236 --> 01:05:42.367
Hold on.


01:05:42.503 --> 01:05:44.299
[engine revs]


01:05:45.471 --> 01:05:46.566
Whoo!


01:05:47.068 --> 01:05:48.099
[inhales sharply]


01:05:48.568 --> 01:05:50.338
Oh, that's a woman
after my heart.


01:05:50.473 --> 01:05:52.978
-[laughs] I love driving!
-I don't wanna...


01:05:53.113 --> 01:05:55.209
I don't know who
taught you how to drive


01:05:55.345 --> 01:05:57.780
-but they weren't good.
-[tires squeal]


01:05:57.916 --> 01:06:00.313
[♪ pop music playing]


01:06:00.449 --> 01:06:02.620
Wrong side! Wrong
side! Wrong side!


01:06:03.189 --> 01:06:05.582
-[Tess] Okay.
-You're gonna get us killed!


01:06:05.718 --> 01:06:07.458
-[horns honking]
-[Anna] Oh, geez.


01:06:07.593 --> 01:06:08.862
[screams]


01:06:11.064 --> 01:06:12.859
Oh! I can't look. I can't look.


01:06:13.328 --> 01:06:14.762
No, no. I'm a very good driver.


01:06:14.898 --> 01:06:16.496
[Anna screams]


01:06:21.343 --> 01:06:23.371
[both screaming]


01:06:29.682 --> 01:06:31.984
That was smashing.


01:06:34.884 --> 01:06:36.516
[Anna] Whoo!


01:06:42.929 --> 01:06:44.790
-[Tess] Oh!
-[tires screech]


01:06:44.926 --> 01:06:46.033
Hi.


01:06:46.469 --> 01:06:48.665
Hi. [chuckles] Nice car.


01:06:48.800 --> 01:06:50.102
It's totally mine.


01:06:50.237 --> 01:06:52.067
-[Anna] You think he's cute.
-[Tess] I do not.


01:06:52.202 --> 01:06:53.700
-You totally do.
-Stop. I do not.


01:06:53.836 --> 01:06:55.991
-[Anna] Yes, you do. You do.
-[Tess] I do not. Shut up.


01:06:56.074 --> 01:06:56.870
[Anna] She thinks you're cute!


01:06:57.005 --> 01:06:58.005
I do not!


01:06:58.107 --> 01:06:59.039
-Yes, she does.
-I do.


01:06:59.175 --> 01:07:00.474
-She so does.
-I do.


01:07:00.876 --> 01:07:02.172
Thanks.


01:07:02.307 --> 01:07:03.510
Dr. Coleman?


01:07:04.353 --> 01:07:05.611
Oh, my gosh. Go.


01:07:06.214 --> 01:07:07.750
That's my therapist!


01:07:07.886 --> 01:07:09.716
[Anna] You nervous?


01:07:09.852 --> 01:07:12.457
[Eric] Oh, why would I be?
We're perfect for each other.


01:07:12.592 --> 01:07:13.621
You'll see.


01:07:14.057 --> 01:07:15.896
Oh, that's cryptic.


01:07:16.031 --> 01:07:17.782
-[Anna clears throat]
-[worker] Coleman/Reyes?


01:07:17.865 --> 01:07:20.263
-Ah, yes. That's us.
-Go.


01:07:21.402 --> 01:07:22.402
My love.


01:07:22.505 --> 01:07:23.505
[Anna clears throat]


01:07:23.639 --> 01:07:25.367
-So many ruffles.
-Yeah.


01:07:26.301 --> 01:07:28.304
-There we go.
-Ah.


01:07:29.543 --> 01:07:30.835
How are you?


01:07:30.970 --> 01:07:33.612
Oh, um, I was just dumped
by my fiancé, so...


01:07:33.747 --> 01:07:34.975
-You know.
-Oh, no.


01:07:35.110 --> 01:07:37.147
I... I'm so sorry.


01:07:37.283 --> 01:07:39.913
Oh, what a decent thing
to say. Thank you.


01:07:40.048 --> 01:07:40.949
Yes, of course.


01:07:41.085 --> 01:07:43.046
Are you single? [chuckles]


01:07:43.182 --> 01:07:44.485
Kidding!


01:07:45.387 --> 01:07:47.594
Um, can I see your paperwork?


01:07:47.730 --> 01:07:48.825
-Ah, yes.
-[worker] Yeah.


01:07:48.961 --> 01:07:49.961
I'm sure you're approved.


01:07:50.058 --> 01:07:51.527
Wait. Whoa.


01:07:51.662 --> 01:07:52.848
Don't you need to see if
we really know each other?


01:07:52.931 --> 01:07:54.198
I mean, usually, yeah,


01:07:54.334 --> 01:07:58.571
but he seems like such
a kind and honest man


01:07:58.706 --> 01:07:59.936
who clearly works out.


01:08:00.072 --> 01:08:01.539
-Oh.
-A lot. [chuckles]


01:08:02.008 --> 01:08:03.239
I mean you could be a gymnast.


01:08:03.375 --> 01:08:05.043
I did once qualify
to represent the UK


01:08:05.179 --> 01:08:06.656
-in pole vaulting.
-You're kidding. Really?


01:08:06.739 --> 01:08:07.981
I'd still like for us to prove


01:08:08.116 --> 01:08:10.549
that we, you know,
are marriage material.


01:08:11.085 --> 01:08:13.987
So, what's my favorite
road trip snack?


01:08:14.122 --> 01:08:16.917
Uh, 7-Eleven hot dog
dipped in blue Slurpee.


01:08:17.052 --> 01:08:18.187
Dream vacay?


01:08:18.323 --> 01:08:19.859
Taking the girls
to the Galapagos.


01:08:19.995 --> 01:08:22.194
Harper would love
the biodiversity


01:08:22.329 --> 01:08:24.369
and I think Lily could
really benefit from the dirt.


01:08:24.496 --> 01:08:27.567
Though she really just
wants to see a, uh...


01:08:27.703 --> 01:08:30.031
Komodo dragon in the wild.


01:08:30.167 --> 01:08:31.702
It's her favorite animal.


01:08:31.838 --> 01:08:33.730
These are too, too easy.


01:08:33.866 --> 01:08:35.437
You gotta hit me
with the hard stuff.


01:08:35.572 --> 01:08:39.069
What is my guilty
pleasure pump-up song?


01:08:39.205 --> 01:08:40.277
Oh.


01:08:40.412 --> 01:08:43.344
Uh, darling, I promised
to never divulge


01:08:43.480 --> 01:08:44.946
that highly-classified
information.


01:08:45.082 --> 01:08:47.048
See? He doesn't know me.


01:08:47.184 --> 01:08:48.786
-At all. See?
-Okay.


01:08:48.921 --> 01:08:50.021
We can't get married.


01:08:50.157 --> 01:08:53.290
[groans] It's...
It's Chumbawamba.


01:08:54.387 --> 01:08:55.423
She told you?


01:08:55.559 --> 01:08:57.296
Wait. "Creepy Crawling"
or "Tubthumping"?


01:08:57.432 --> 01:08:59.693
♪ <i>I get knocked down
But I get up again</i> ♪


01:08:59.828 --> 01:09:01.828
♪ <i>You're never
gonna Keep me down</i> ♪


01:09:01.964 --> 01:09:04.434
♪ <i>I get knocked down
But I get up again</i> ♪


01:09:04.569 --> 01:09:06.573
♪ <i>You're never
gonna Keep me down</i> ♪


01:09:06.708 --> 01:09:08.233
That's the one, yeah.


01:09:08.368 --> 01:09:09.634
[chuckles, sighs]


01:09:09.769 --> 01:09:12.410
♪ <i>Pissin' the night away</i> ♪


01:09:12.546 --> 01:09:13.671
Oh, wow.


01:09:13.807 --> 01:09:18.777
♪ <i>Oh, Danny Boy, Danny Boy</i> ♪


01:09:19.722 --> 01:09:20.817
♪ <i>Danny Boy</i> ♪


01:09:20.952 --> 01:09:22.253
[sniffles, groans]


01:09:22.388 --> 01:09:24.820
-Danny was my fiancé's name.
-Okay, enough.


01:09:25.423 --> 01:09:27.392
What's my deepest, darkest fear?


01:09:27.528 --> 01:09:28.528
Oh.


01:09:29.121 --> 01:09:31.560
That your love for Harper
and need to protect her


01:09:31.695 --> 01:09:34.468
will push her away rather
than bring her close.


01:09:35.071 --> 01:09:36.829
And then she'll run
away and be a surf bum


01:09:36.964 --> 01:09:38.723
and then she'll get a
dodgy tattoo of the sun


01:09:38.806 --> 01:09:40.205
around her belly button.


01:09:41.441 --> 01:09:45.645
But you're a phenomenal
mum and Harper is amazing,


01:09:45.781 --> 01:09:47.575
so that will never happen.


01:09:51.314 --> 01:09:53.586
Well, that was really sweet.


01:09:53.722 --> 01:09:55.151
I didn't know that.


01:09:55.720 --> 01:09:57.440
[worker] You know, I approve
hundreds of marriages


01:09:57.523 --> 01:10:00.225
that... [scoffs] ...probably
won't even last a year.


01:10:00.794 --> 01:10:02.293
But you two...


01:10:08.499 --> 01:10:10.895
-Thank you.
-[clears throat] Next.


01:10:13.303 --> 01:10:15.308
Well done. We got approved.


01:10:15.444 --> 01:10:16.505
Ugh.


01:10:16.640 --> 01:10:19.176
Ugh, my seafood vendor
says we canceled.


01:10:19.312 --> 01:10:20.672
-I should deal with this.
-Bet.


01:10:20.808 --> 01:10:22.579
-Yeah, my mom's almost here.
-Okay.


01:10:22.715 --> 01:10:24.716
Uh, bye.


01:10:24.852 --> 01:10:25.650
What an odd mix-up.


01:10:25.785 --> 01:10:27.952
[tires screech]


01:10:28.087 --> 01:10:30.055
Hop in, muppet. How'd it go?


01:10:30.191 --> 01:10:32.755
Your dad knows a
lot about my mom.


01:10:32.891 --> 01:10:34.910
-I think he really loves her.
-[Tess] But did you do enough


01:10:34.993 --> 01:10:36.588
to break them up?


01:10:36.723 --> 01:10:37.960
-I don't know.
-[groans]


01:10:38.096 --> 01:10:39.528
I need to clear my mind.


01:10:39.663 --> 01:10:42.631
-Can we go somewhere?
-Yes, yeah. Get in.


01:10:42.766 --> 01:10:45.398
-[Anna] Don't drive so fast.
-[Tess] Okay. Buckle up!


01:10:45.534 --> 01:10:47.537
-[engine revs]
-[Anna screams]


01:10:47.672 --> 01:10:49.325
[Harper] "Change the
hearts you know are wrong


01:10:49.408 --> 01:10:50.788
to reach the place
where you belong."


01:10:50.871 --> 01:10:52.440
What do you think
she meant by that?


01:10:52.575 --> 01:10:53.947
[Lily] I think she
made it all up,


01:10:54.083 --> 01:10:55.198
but look on the
bright side, honey,


01:10:55.281 --> 01:10:57.611
these scooters are so much fun!


01:10:57.746 --> 01:10:58.972
Why have we never
done this before?


01:10:59.055 --> 01:11:00.578
Because you already
have one fake hip


01:11:00.713 --> 01:11:02.089
and you do not need another.


01:11:02.224 --> 01:11:04.650
Very funny. I'll have
you know, in this body,


01:11:04.786 --> 01:11:07.285
I have two real hips. [screams]


01:11:07.420 --> 01:11:08.828
[laughing]


01:11:08.964 --> 01:11:11.121
-[vendor] Whoa!
-[screams]


01:11:11.824 --> 01:11:14.200
[Harper groans] Sorry. Sorry.


01:11:16.595 --> 01:11:17.830
Nothing broke!


01:11:19.433 --> 01:11:20.364
We're invincible!


01:11:20.500 --> 01:11:21.432
Bone density!


01:11:21.567 --> 01:11:23.209
I'm not exhausted!


01:11:23.678 --> 01:11:25.343
[both laughing]


01:11:26.643 --> 01:11:31.448
-Girls, get in the car.
-[phone chiming]


01:11:33.420 --> 01:11:36.123
How do kids get away
with anything anymore?


01:11:43.556 --> 01:11:45.022
[Tess screams]


01:11:51.570 --> 01:11:54.438
You know, I hated you
a little less today.


01:11:56.204 --> 01:11:58.809
I think it's hard to hate me
when I look like your gran.


01:11:58.944 --> 01:12:00.008
[chuckles]


01:12:00.144 --> 01:12:01.379
[Tess] And...


01:12:02.448 --> 01:12:05.548
I hated you a little
less today too.


01:12:10.251 --> 01:12:13.959
I just don't understand how
anyone can dislike California.


01:12:14.094 --> 01:12:15.855
It's, like, a wrong opinion.


01:12:17.265 --> 01:12:19.523
Harper, you can't
have a wrong opinion.


01:12:19.659 --> 01:12:21.331
I mean, look around.


01:12:21.466 --> 01:12:25.330
Yes. Okay, Harper, it's lovely.


01:12:25.465 --> 01:12:26.965
It's lovely.


01:12:27.533 --> 01:12:28.802
I just...


01:12:29.809 --> 01:12:31.475
[sighs]


01:12:32.176 --> 01:12:34.005
...I miss England.


01:12:40.112 --> 01:12:42.882
We can talk about
her if you want.


01:12:45.419 --> 01:12:46.490
No, thanks.


01:12:48.722 --> 01:12:50.356
I think if I talk about her,


01:12:51.158 --> 01:12:53.365
I'm giving away what
little of her I have left.


01:12:55.703 --> 01:12:56.929
Okay.


01:12:58.507 --> 01:13:03.833
And why are you so obsessed
that I like Los Angeles?


01:13:03.969 --> 01:13:05.844
-Well, I'm not.
-Yes, you are.


01:13:05.979 --> 01:13:07.180
-No.
-Yes.


01:13:07.649 --> 01:13:11.878
And look, even if I liked it
a little bit here, I mean...


01:13:15.049 --> 01:13:18.449
You... You still
don't want me around.


01:13:18.918 --> 01:13:21.594
-Obviously not.
-Obviously not.


01:13:22.631 --> 01:13:25.331
I guess it's a good thing
we're stopping this wedding.


01:13:26.668 --> 01:13:27.894
Yeah.


01:13:30.101 --> 01:13:31.302
Where are they?


01:13:31.438 --> 01:13:32.798
They're supposed
to be home by now.


01:13:32.901 --> 01:13:35.401
This is very good. A little dry.


01:13:36.203 --> 01:13:39.636
Very fruit-forward. And
by fruit, I mean grapes.


01:13:40.239 --> 01:13:42.948
Your lack of concern,
it's not working.


01:13:43.083 --> 01:13:45.010
Just stay calm, honey.


01:13:45.578 --> 01:13:46.685
Stay calm?


01:13:47.355 --> 01:13:48.711
But I've got the
rehearsal lunch,


01:13:48.847 --> 01:13:49.956
the final dress fitting,


01:13:50.092 --> 01:13:52.084
and my wedding is in 36 hours,


01:13:52.219 --> 01:13:54.221
and I'm trapped in the
body of a ninth-grader.


01:13:54.357 --> 01:13:55.693
[Anna] I did.


01:13:55.829 --> 01:13:57.416
-I told you she approved it.
-You most certainly did not.


01:13:57.499 --> 01:13:59.109
[Anna] What difference
does it make, anyway?


01:13:59.192 --> 01:14:01.026
-It's done now.
-Where on earth have you been?


01:14:02.002 --> 01:14:03.436
-Oh.
-Well.


01:14:03.572 --> 01:14:05.536
Can't two adult women come
home when they please?


01:14:05.672 --> 01:14:07.190
What do you think you're
doing driving around


01:14:07.273 --> 01:14:08.505
like that with Ella all day?


01:14:08.641 --> 01:14:10.506
Ella needs to talk
to you, by the way.


01:14:10.642 --> 01:14:12.030
You need to give
her more attention.


01:14:12.113 --> 01:14:13.412
Why am I dressed like that?


01:14:13.547 --> 01:14:15.315
I need more attention
from you sometimes.


01:14:15.451 --> 01:14:16.860
She has a lot of stuff
to talk to you about.


01:14:16.943 --> 01:14:18.208
-[shushes]
-She was crying.


01:14:18.343 --> 01:14:19.913
Okay, I don't care
about that right now.


01:14:20.048 --> 01:14:21.306
Did you make it to the
immigration interview?


01:14:21.389 --> 01:14:23.488
Yes, I did. Just,
like, chill, okay?


01:14:23.623 --> 01:14:26.326
Or do your weird breathing
stuff that you do.


01:14:26.761 --> 01:14:27.987
Chill?


01:14:29.228 --> 01:14:30.789
I am the adult here.


01:14:30.924 --> 01:14:32.866
-I'm in charge.
-[both scoff]


01:14:33.001 --> 01:14:34.268
Doesn't look like it.


01:14:34.403 --> 01:14:36.298
You just earned
yourselves a consequence.


01:14:36.434 --> 01:14:38.662
-Ooh. No.
-Oh, no.


01:14:38.798 --> 01:14:39.697
Give me your phones.


01:14:39.832 --> 01:14:40.901
-Sure.
-[Tess] No.


01:14:41.336 --> 01:14:42.674
Psych.


01:14:42.810 --> 01:14:44.689
By the way, you're the reason
this is all falling apart.


01:14:44.772 --> 01:14:46.004
[Anna] Shut up. No, I'm not.


01:14:46.140 --> 01:14:47.660
[Tess] Yes, it totally
is. And don't...


01:14:47.774 --> 01:14:49.248
Girls, this is serious.


01:14:49.383 --> 01:14:50.878
We all need to
start getting along


01:14:51.013 --> 01:14:52.638
unless we want to be
stuck like this forever.


01:14:52.721 --> 01:14:55.555
You know, you lot are getting
the better end of this deal.


01:14:55.690 --> 01:14:58.758
It's us who are gonna be
dead in, like, five years.


01:14:58.893 --> 01:14:59.826
She's 37.


01:14:59.961 --> 01:15:01.854
I'm 36 and a half!


01:15:01.990 --> 01:15:03.753
While you two were
out having fun,


01:15:03.889 --> 01:15:05.289
we found Madame Jen.


01:15:05.424 --> 01:15:07.725
And she made us buy
business cards for everyone


01:15:07.860 --> 01:15:09.126
and a Reiki ten-pack!


01:15:09.261 --> 01:15:11.663
What even is Reiki?
Huh? What is it?


01:15:11.799 --> 01:15:13.131
Stop talking about Reiki.


01:15:13.267 --> 01:15:15.132
Well, Madame Jen said
to change your hearts,


01:15:15.267 --> 01:15:16.937
so change your
freaking dang hearts.


01:15:17.072 --> 01:15:18.992
It's the only way for us
to get out of this mess.


01:15:19.107 --> 01:15:21.214
I'm switching to
red. Do you want one?


01:15:21.349 --> 01:15:23.411
You're making Mommy
very stressed!


01:15:23.547 --> 01:15:25.546
...use Reiki now! [sighs]


01:15:25.682 --> 01:15:27.286
[♪ Moody pop music plays]


01:15:27.422 --> 01:15:30.357
♪ <i>You think that I'll leave</i> ♪


01:15:31.093 --> 01:15:33.921
♪ <i>Don't worry</i> ♪


01:15:36.330 --> 01:15:39.229
♪ <i>I just keep on</i> ♪


01:15:39.365 --> 01:15:42.234
♪ <i>Coming back</i> ♪


01:15:42.670 --> 01:15:47.933
♪ <i>I'm your good
And I'm your bad</i> ♪


01:15:48.068 --> 01:15:52.138
♪ <i>'Cause you're my baby</i> ♪


01:15:52.273 --> 01:15:57.578
♪ <i>Ooh, oh 'Cause
you're my baby</i> ♪


01:15:57.713 --> 01:16:01.047
♪ <i>Baby Baby</i> ♪


01:16:11.389 --> 01:16:15.067
[Eric] Okay,<i> Blue
Crush.</i> Look at you.


01:16:15.203 --> 01:16:17.536
Shredding the waves, dude.


01:16:17.671 --> 01:16:20.106
-Never use those words again.
-[chuckles]


01:16:20.242 --> 01:16:22.402
Wait, what are you doing here?


01:16:22.537 --> 01:16:23.839
Our lessons.


01:16:25.145 --> 01:16:26.472
What lessons?


01:16:26.608 --> 01:16:27.777
Surf lessons.


01:16:28.811 --> 01:16:29.995
But it looks like you're ready


01:16:30.078 --> 01:16:31.815
to surprise Harper
and take her out.


01:16:31.950 --> 01:16:34.788
Oh, yeah. That's really
gonna surprise Harper.


01:16:35.257 --> 01:16:36.653
-Obviously.
-[chuckles]


01:16:36.788 --> 01:16:38.990
Oh, no, I just ate
a bowl of onions.


01:16:39.126 --> 01:16:40.452
In the water?


01:16:40.921 --> 01:16:42.154
Yeah, they keep me alert.


01:16:42.821 --> 01:16:44.123
[chuckles]


01:16:44.657 --> 01:16:45.960
Okay.


01:16:47.895 --> 01:16:51.600
Look, I know it feels like


01:16:51.735 --> 01:16:54.339
we're in an
impossible situation.


01:16:54.874 --> 01:16:58.302
Maybe that's why things
have felt a bit off with us.


01:16:59.079 --> 01:17:00.546
Yeah, probably.


01:17:01.115 --> 01:17:03.846
Yeah, but Anna...


01:17:05.749 --> 01:17:09.885
I think we should stay in LA.


01:17:11.685 --> 01:17:12.921
What about Lily?


01:17:14.959 --> 01:17:17.023
Going back to London,
to Pembridge Hall,


01:17:17.159 --> 01:17:18.788
it's not going to
bring back her mum.


01:17:19.558 --> 01:17:23.264
And there's no one
keeping us there anymore.


01:17:23.900 --> 01:17:26.906
If I'm honest,
we've felt so lost.


01:17:27.609 --> 01:17:30.076
So what she needs is
to be with family.


01:17:30.712 --> 01:17:34.976
A gran like Tess, a sister
like Harper, and you.


01:17:38.548 --> 01:17:40.454
[sighs, chuckles]


01:17:41.880 --> 01:17:43.018
What is it?


01:17:43.420 --> 01:17:44.451
It's just...


01:17:45.254 --> 01:17:48.895
I can't believe how much
you love me and my family.


01:17:49.631 --> 01:17:53.857
It's a real, true love.
It's just... It's crazy.


01:17:54.427 --> 01:17:57.329
Okay. Well, you made
it look so easy.


01:17:57.865 --> 01:17:59.099
I'm gonna give it a go.


01:17:59.768 --> 01:18:00.967
I don't know if that's...


01:18:01.103 --> 01:18:02.463
Maybe I've improved
as much as you!


01:18:04.539 --> 01:18:05.539
[groans]


01:18:05.639 --> 01:18:06.639
Oh!


01:18:06.741 --> 01:18:08.405
I'm okay! [groans]


01:18:08.884 --> 01:18:10.110
Oh.


01:18:11.814 --> 01:18:13.243
[Eric] No. I'm gonna wait.


01:18:13.378 --> 01:18:15.249
I'm gonna wait for
the instructor.


01:18:15.752 --> 01:18:17.181
I mean, you were amazing.


01:18:17.317 --> 01:18:18.917
You were, like,
weaving and dodging,


01:18:19.053 --> 01:18:20.784
and you're like a pro surfer.


01:18:21.420 --> 01:18:23.553
-I'm glad we talked.
-Yeah, me too.


01:18:24.556 --> 01:18:26.157
[Eric] It's good we
came to a decision.


01:18:26.292 --> 01:18:27.859
[Anna] Yeah, dude. Really good.


01:18:28.395 --> 01:18:29.932
[Eric] See you at
the rehearsal lunch!


01:18:30.067 --> 01:18:32.539
[Anna] Totally, but my
mom said I have to...


01:18:35.840 --> 01:18:37.733
It fits perfectly.
Anna, come look.


01:18:37.869 --> 01:18:39.374
Oh, wow.


01:18:39.509 --> 01:18:40.543
[clears throat]


01:18:41.012 --> 01:18:45.310
Sweetheart... [sniffles]
...fix your posture.


01:18:46.088 --> 01:18:47.312
This is weird.


01:18:48.147 --> 01:18:50.056
Weirder for me, trust me.


01:18:50.192 --> 01:18:51.314
Really? Are you the one


01:18:51.450 --> 01:18:53.089
wearing your mom's
wedding dress?


01:18:53.225 --> 01:18:55.821
Well, I never thought I'd
get to have this experience.


01:18:55.956 --> 01:18:57.330
Especially like this.


01:18:57.999 --> 01:19:00.600
[Anna] Well, Mom, you know how
much I love to wear a dress.


01:19:00.735 --> 01:19:03.494
[Harper] Ugh. Sorry this
is such a mess, Harper.


01:19:03.630 --> 01:19:06.232
[Anna] Mom, there's
something I need to tell you.


01:19:11.604 --> 01:19:14.271
What were you talking to
my dad about this morning?


01:19:14.407 --> 01:19:17.375
Oh, we were just
talking about the lunch.


01:19:18.143 --> 01:19:19.448
What about the lunch?


01:19:19.583 --> 01:19:20.884
Just lunch stuff.


01:19:24.919 --> 01:19:27.752
Oh, right. The lunch.


01:19:27.887 --> 01:19:29.123
[Anna chuckles]


01:19:29.955 --> 01:19:32.159
Okay. Um.


01:19:33.195 --> 01:19:35.331
I'm just gonna
make a quick call.


01:19:35.466 --> 01:19:36.397
[Anna] Okay.


01:19:36.532 --> 01:19:37.571
Okay.


01:19:40.199 --> 01:19:42.906
[♪ Dramatic music plays]


01:19:52.847 --> 01:19:56.083
Oh, hi! It's Tess.


01:19:56.219 --> 01:20:00.419
Um, listen, last minute
but Anna was wondering


01:20:00.554 --> 01:20:04.095
if you might like to attend
her rehearsal luncheon.


01:20:05.132 --> 01:20:08.565
No, no. You would not be an
imposition. You know what?


01:20:08.701 --> 01:20:09.966
I think your appearance there


01:20:10.101 --> 01:20:12.265
would make it a much
more lively affair.


01:20:15.638 --> 01:20:18.637
[Eric] <i>So, I just wanted to
say that I'm very excited.</i>


01:20:18.773 --> 01:20:21.506
<i>And being at my new restaurant
makes it all the more special</i>


01:20:21.641 --> 01:20:24.144
for all of us to finally
come together as a family.


01:20:24.279 --> 01:20:27.384
So with that said,
welcome to Lily's.


01:20:27.520 --> 01:20:28.452
[guest] Congratulations.


01:20:28.587 --> 01:20:29.721
Thank you for coming.


01:20:29.856 --> 01:20:31.234
Really, Eric and I
so appreciate it.


01:20:31.317 --> 01:20:32.615
-[server clears throat]
-Oh.


01:20:33.118 --> 01:20:34.353
Right. Thanks.


01:20:35.595 --> 01:20:36.675
[server] Champagne, ladies?


01:20:36.796 --> 01:20:37.836
-Yes, please.
-Yes, please.


01:20:37.962 --> 01:20:39.426
-'Cause we're adults.
-Mm-hmm.


01:20:39.562 --> 01:20:42.260
Girls, Eric's parents are
here so best behavior, please.


01:20:42.396 --> 01:20:44.199
Stand up straight. Good posture.


01:20:44.335 --> 01:20:49.474
Anna, my soon-to-be daughter.
My heart is so full.


01:20:49.609 --> 01:20:51.139
[Anna] That's me. [chuckles]


01:20:51.742 --> 01:20:53.208
How was your flight?


01:20:53.343 --> 01:20:56.214
Oh, it was 13 hours and 30
minutes from Manila. Ugh.


01:20:56.350 --> 01:20:57.242
Major jet lag.


01:20:57.377 --> 01:20:59.142
-Some worse than others.
-[snoring]


01:20:59.278 --> 01:21:02.786
But I really love it here.


01:21:02.921 --> 01:21:04.281
Maybe Harper can
teach me the surf.


01:21:04.386 --> 01:21:07.023
-Sure, dude.
-<i> Mano po, Lola</i>.


01:21:08.158 --> 01:21:10.961
You're so silly. Only
Lily calls me Lola.


01:21:11.097 --> 01:21:13.726
But I want to support
your Tagalog learning.


01:21:13.861 --> 01:21:15.299
Keep it up.


01:21:15.435 --> 01:21:16.627
Come on, Anna.


01:21:16.762 --> 01:21:18.284
-Let's have a drink.
-No, no, no, no. We just...


01:21:18.367 --> 01:21:19.887
We have to wait for
the surprise guest.


01:21:20.233 --> 01:21:21.470
What are you talking about?


01:21:21.606 --> 01:21:23.039
Oh, just wait.


01:21:23.174 --> 01:21:26.369
-Hello, sir. Welcome.
-Ah, no, thank you.


01:21:26.505 --> 01:21:28.343
-I'm here to see someone.
-Jake?


01:21:28.879 --> 01:21:30.041
[server 2] Just alone or...


01:21:30.176 --> 01:21:31.509
What's he doing here?


01:21:31.645 --> 01:21:33.167
I invited him but I
didn't think he'd come.


01:21:33.250 --> 01:21:35.046
But, you know, he
really likes your gran.


01:21:35.182 --> 01:21:36.479
My mom's gonna freak out,


01:21:36.615 --> 01:21:38.106
-you know that?
-I know. So will my dad.


01:21:38.189 --> 01:21:40.724
-That was the whole point.
-[groans] You...


01:21:40.859 --> 01:21:44.930
Dr. C. Thank you
for inviting me.


01:21:45.065 --> 01:21:47.727
I... I saved your number.
I hope that's okay.


01:21:47.862 --> 01:21:49.562
Of course.


01:21:50.131 --> 01:21:51.463
-Hi, there.
-Hey.


01:21:51.599 --> 01:21:53.632
Hmm. I think I'm gonna
have to ask you to leave.


01:21:53.768 --> 01:21:55.436
Uh, now?


01:21:55.572 --> 01:21:58.776
But, uh, you know, your mom,
she really wanted me here.


01:21:58.911 --> 01:22:01.913
Right. I'm sure.
[chuckles] Well...


01:22:03.383 --> 01:22:05.481
[whispers]


01:22:05.616 --> 01:22:06.645
[Anna] Okay.


01:22:07.382 --> 01:22:09.052
-I got you.
-Thank you so much.


01:22:09.188 --> 01:22:10.904
-[Tess] No, no, no. Wait.
-You're the best, bro.


01:22:10.987 --> 01:22:11.919
-Wait!
-Thank goodness.


01:22:12.054 --> 01:22:13.320
[Jake] I will be right back.


01:22:13.456 --> 01:22:15.142
-[Tess] No. Jake, don't go.
-Ah, Tess. Tess.


01:22:15.225 --> 01:22:16.892
-Yes?
-Uh, can we have a chat later?


01:22:17.027 --> 01:22:18.589
-It's regarding Lily.
-Oh!


01:22:18.724 --> 01:22:21.093
If it's regarding Lily,
we should chat now.


01:22:21.228 --> 01:22:22.394
[Harry] My big sister, Anna.


01:22:22.530 --> 01:22:25.068
After every atomic
wedgie you gave me,


01:22:25.204 --> 01:22:28.200
I always knew that you
also had an atomic heart.


01:22:28.335 --> 01:22:29.809
-Cheers.
-[guests] Cheers!


01:22:29.945 --> 01:22:33.142
Anna and I decided we
should all stay in LA.


01:22:34.677 --> 01:22:35.446
What?


01:22:35.582 --> 01:22:37.117
-Yes.
-What?


01:22:37.252 --> 01:22:37.977
Everyone?


01:22:38.113 --> 01:22:39.713
-Yes.
-[Tess stammers]


01:22:39.848 --> 01:22:40.950
As a therapist,


01:22:41.085 --> 01:22:42.547
I was hoping to
get your thoughts


01:22:42.682 --> 01:22:44.549
on the best way to
approach it with Lily.


01:22:46.686 --> 01:22:48.593
But, I know how you feel
about billable hours


01:22:48.728 --> 01:22:50.692
so we can chat later. Yeah?


01:22:50.827 --> 01:22:52.056
[Tess] Okay. Okay.


01:22:52.192 --> 01:22:53.932
[breathing heavily]


01:23:00.568 --> 01:23:04.269
You bloody backstabber.
I know what you did.


01:23:04.404 --> 01:23:05.443
-Shh!
-[Harry] All right,


01:23:05.579 --> 01:23:06.712
who wants to speak next?


01:23:06.848 --> 01:23:08.244
Father of the groom looks ready.


01:23:08.379 --> 01:23:10.543
No, no. I have a few
choice words for the bride.


01:23:10.678 --> 01:23:12.558
-I would like to make a toast.
-[glass clinking]


01:23:12.650 --> 01:23:13.785
That's crystal.


01:23:13.921 --> 01:23:15.213
Uh, we have a toasting triangle.


01:23:15.348 --> 01:23:16.885
-Oh, piss off.
-Okay.


01:23:17.521 --> 01:23:20.253
I would like to make a
toast to your future husband


01:23:20.388 --> 01:23:23.627
so that he knows
what kind of woman


01:23:23.763 --> 01:23:24.995
he is getting married to.


01:23:25.130 --> 01:23:27.994
[chuckles] He does,
he does, he does.


01:23:28.130 --> 01:23:29.702
He knows who he's marrying


01:23:29.837 --> 01:23:31.267
and he can make
his own decisions


01:23:31.403 --> 01:23:34.140
and he knows not to be
manipulated by other people.


01:23:34.275 --> 01:23:35.202
Tess.


01:23:35.338 --> 01:23:37.873
Hey, gramps, this is between us.


01:23:38.009 --> 01:23:39.345
[Anna] Listen to your husband.


01:23:39.481 --> 01:23:41.439
[Tess] You listen to me.


01:23:41.575 --> 01:23:43.274
[Harper] Ugh, Ella.
What does she want?


01:23:43.710 --> 01:23:46.044
Micro cilantro from the
foothills of Oaxaca.


01:23:46.180 --> 01:23:47.686
It was not my fault.


01:23:48.088 --> 01:23:51.016
That micro cilantro is
bursting with flavor.


01:23:51.152 --> 01:23:52.319
But it is your fault


01:23:52.455 --> 01:23:55.687
that the cilantro
has no loyalty to...


01:23:55.823 --> 01:23:58.190
-[Lily] What are they doing?
-We have to stop them.


01:23:58.326 --> 01:23:59.855
Are you doing all right, Harp?


01:23:59.991 --> 01:24:02.896
[sighs] Ella, this is
the last thing I need.


01:24:03.032 --> 01:24:04.270
Oh, Jake's back already.


01:24:04.405 --> 01:24:05.405
Jake? Who?


01:24:05.500 --> 01:24:07.200
Jake, what... What
are you doing here?


01:24:07.336 --> 01:24:09.001
-Uh...
-It was all her, I swear.


01:24:09.137 --> 01:24:11.005
Hello. Um, and you are?


01:24:11.140 --> 01:24:13.011
That's Anna's ex-boyfriend.


01:24:13.146 --> 01:24:15.710
-What? Why?
-She invited her ex-boyfriend?


01:24:15.846 --> 01:24:17.048
[guests] What?


01:24:17.183 --> 01:24:18.497
Because she still
has feelings for him.


01:24:18.580 --> 01:24:20.100
-Okay. That's not... That...
-[Lily] No.


01:24:20.183 --> 01:24:21.882
-What? I...
-No. Uh...


01:24:22.018 --> 01:24:23.285
After the appetizer,


01:24:23.420 --> 01:24:25.171
Anna said she wasn't
feeling well so I went...


01:24:25.254 --> 01:24:26.993
Right. I wasn't feeling well.


01:24:27.863 --> 01:24:29.040
Okay, but not from
the food here.


01:24:29.123 --> 01:24:30.190
The food is fine.


01:24:30.325 --> 01:24:31.958
-Too fishy. No.
-It's fish.


01:24:32.094 --> 01:24:33.899
It is not the food.


01:24:34.035 --> 01:24:36.435
She's just on her
period. That's all.


01:24:36.571 --> 01:24:38.069
She's on her period.


01:24:38.936 --> 01:24:40.036
I'm on mine right now.


01:24:40.171 --> 01:24:41.371
-I got it.
-I didn't know where


01:24:41.503 --> 01:24:42.526
-you are in your cycle...
-I know, dude.


01:24:42.609 --> 01:24:43.743
It's fine. Thanks.


01:24:43.879 --> 01:24:45.127
Can someone please explain to me


01:24:45.210 --> 01:24:46.591
-what's going on here.
-I don't know.


01:24:46.674 --> 01:24:48.411
-Let's just tell the truth.
-Don't let her.


01:24:48.547 --> 01:24:51.012
She shouldn't explain anything
because she will just lie.


01:24:51.147 --> 01:24:52.551
-Hey, me?
-She lies.


01:24:52.686 --> 01:24:54.548
-Yeah.
-I trusted you.


01:24:54.683 --> 01:24:57.318
I know, but you don't
know what he said to me.


01:24:57.454 --> 01:24:59.391
You weren't there.
You didn't hear it.


01:25:00.193 --> 01:25:02.491
I don't think this
marriage should happen.


01:25:02.627 --> 01:25:05.359
Well, you know what? It's
not just about what you want.


01:25:05.495 --> 01:25:07.135
It's about what she
wants and she wants...


01:25:07.232 --> 01:25:08.512
It isn't ever about what I want.


01:25:08.629 --> 01:25:10.359
-It's always about you.
-That's enough.


01:25:10.495 --> 01:25:11.602
Does everyone want this?


01:25:11.738 --> 01:25:12.738
Okay, that's enough.


01:25:12.872 --> 01:25:14.038
Well, yes. Some of them do.


01:25:14.174 --> 01:25:15.832
-[dishes clatter]
-Hey, that's enough!


01:25:19.837 --> 01:25:22.075
The girls fighting is one thing


01:25:22.210 --> 01:25:23.516
but this is your mum.


01:25:24.152 --> 01:25:26.986
And for some reason, your
ex-boyfriend is here.


01:25:27.949 --> 01:25:28.750
Yeah.


01:25:28.885 --> 01:25:31.316
Anna, I love you


01:25:31.719 --> 01:25:34.422
but you're clearly
having second thoughts.


01:25:36.558 --> 01:25:38.889
This isn't working
for our families,


01:25:39.024 --> 01:25:42.100
and we always said we'd
put our families first.


01:25:42.964 --> 01:25:44.201
So...


01:25:47.641 --> 01:25:48.865
We can't do this.


01:25:51.105 --> 01:25:52.575
I can't do this.


01:25:52.710 --> 01:25:53.776
[sobs]


01:25:54.745 --> 01:25:58.116
Lily, help your grandparents.
I'll meet you at the valet.


01:25:58.817 --> 01:26:00.052
The wedding's off.


01:26:01.516 --> 01:26:03.847
[crying] He's right. It's over.


01:26:04.448 --> 01:26:05.486
[Anna] Wait, no.


01:26:06.619 --> 01:26:07.741
Wait, please, please, please.


01:26:07.824 --> 01:26:08.626
No.


01:26:08.762 --> 01:26:09.994
I'm so sorry. I promise,


01:26:10.130 --> 01:26:11.888
I didn't mean for
this to happen.


01:26:13.900 --> 01:26:15.265
[whispers] I think you did.


01:26:20.771 --> 01:26:21.702
Well.


01:26:21.838 --> 01:26:23.801
[crying]


01:26:25.245 --> 01:26:28.476
-I guess we did it.
-Yeah. [chuckles]


01:26:35.489 --> 01:26:36.416
Uh...


01:26:36.552 --> 01:26:38.185
I know this isn't the best time


01:26:38.320 --> 01:26:40.721
but can I have my car back?


01:26:40.857 --> 01:26:42.160
[scoffs]


01:26:46.457 --> 01:26:47.858
Maybe later.


01:26:50.100 --> 01:26:52.104
[emotional music plays]


01:27:00.514 --> 01:27:01.575
[sighs]


01:27:06.344 --> 01:27:07.383
Mom!


01:27:10.052 --> 01:27:11.520
She seems upset.


01:27:12.223 --> 01:27:14.192
No, she just needs some space.


01:27:18.264 --> 01:27:21.399
What about you?
Are you doing okay?


01:27:21.935 --> 01:27:24.037
Oh, yeah. I'm always okay.


01:27:25.830 --> 01:27:27.898
It would be fair if you weren't.


01:27:28.667 --> 01:27:31.374
That all got pretty crazy.


01:27:34.210 --> 01:27:35.676
I worry what will happen


01:27:35.811 --> 01:27:38.975
when Tess doesn't have those
two to drive her crazy.


01:27:40.921 --> 01:27:42.880
You're worried about her?


01:27:45.853 --> 01:27:47.855
I'm worried Tess
would be really lonely


01:27:48.358 --> 01:27:50.252
if all of you moved to London.


01:27:50.388 --> 01:27:51.823
[sighs]


01:27:52.624 --> 01:27:54.496
You're a good guy, Ryan.


01:27:56.595 --> 01:27:58.401
Thank you. [chuckles]


01:27:59.298 --> 01:28:00.598
Go on.


01:28:00.733 --> 01:28:02.834
Maybe this isn't for me to fix.


01:28:05.579 --> 01:28:06.805
[sighs]


01:28:10.785 --> 01:28:12.415
Mind if I join you?


01:28:13.346 --> 01:28:14.417
[sniffles]


01:28:15.856 --> 01:28:17.849
-Okay.
-Okay.


01:28:19.923 --> 01:28:21.226
[sighs]


01:28:21.927 --> 01:28:23.195
Are you okay?


01:28:26.123 --> 01:28:28.398
I haven't seen my
dad that upset...


01:28:31.167 --> 01:28:32.798
since my mum died.


01:28:36.569 --> 01:28:38.111
And it was all my fault.


01:28:40.237 --> 01:28:44.843
You know, when Ryan
asked me to marry him,


01:28:46.480 --> 01:28:47.912
I thought a lot about


01:28:48.047 --> 01:28:50.255
what Anna and Harry's
dad would have said.


01:28:52.259 --> 01:28:54.083
How he would have felt about it.


01:28:55.326 --> 01:28:57.955
I think he'd be so happy for us.


01:28:59.499 --> 01:29:03.702
That we found someone
who loved us all so much.


01:29:03.837 --> 01:29:05.435
[breathes shakily]


01:29:13.940 --> 01:29:15.613
I think my mum would
feel the same way.


01:29:15.748 --> 01:29:16.945
Yeah.


01:29:17.915 --> 01:29:22.120
-[sobs] I really miss her.
-[cries] I know. It's okay.


01:29:22.256 --> 01:29:23.989
She would be so
disappointed in me.


01:29:24.124 --> 01:29:26.256
-No, no, no.
-Yes, she would.


01:29:26.391 --> 01:29:29.527
Because I was very
selfish. I was.


01:29:29.663 --> 01:29:30.554
No.


01:29:30.689 --> 01:29:33.496
I was, and I know it.


01:29:34.331 --> 01:29:39.029
No, she'd know your heart.


01:29:39.839 --> 01:29:41.097
[sniffles]


01:29:42.536 --> 01:29:43.943
I just... I should...


01:29:44.078 --> 01:29:46.069
-Find my dad...
-[Lily] Yeah.


01:29:47.178 --> 01:29:48.907
...and... and apologize.


01:29:56.984 --> 01:29:59.758
[audience chanting]
<i>Ella, Ella, Ella.</i>


01:29:59.893 --> 01:30:02.387
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:02.522 --> 01:30:04.928
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:05.063 --> 01:30:07.833
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:08.202 --> 01:30:10.595
[Anna] Why are you
walking so fast?


01:30:10.730 --> 01:30:12.129
I can't walk as fast as you.


01:30:12.264 --> 01:30:14.048
[Harper] Ella keeps texting
me the word "urgent,"


01:30:14.131 --> 01:30:15.567
and her show starts, like, now.


01:30:15.702 --> 01:30:16.782
[Anna] But what about Eric?


01:30:16.904 --> 01:30:18.233
I think we should go back, Mom.


01:30:18.369 --> 01:30:19.722
I thought there was a way
to make everyone happy


01:30:19.805 --> 01:30:21.071
but there's not, all right?


01:30:21.207 --> 01:30:22.631
But I think that we
should go back for Eric.


01:30:22.714 --> 01:30:25.278
-I really should...
-Come on. My client needs me.


01:30:25.413 --> 01:30:26.609
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:26.744 --> 01:30:29.481
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:29.617 --> 01:30:31.620
[♪ Pop music plays]


01:30:32.423 --> 01:30:33.652
♪ <i>You're my confidant</i> ♪


01:30:33.787 --> 01:30:34.819
♪ <i>You're my underdog</i> ♪


01:30:34.954 --> 01:30:36.095
♪ <i>You're the one I want</i> ♪


01:30:36.231 --> 01:30:37.694
♪ <i>'Til it's said and done</i> ♪


01:30:37.829 --> 01:30:39.498
♪ <i>Call it delicate
All the benefits</i> ♪


01:30:39.633 --> 01:30:41.366
♪ <i>Invisible string
When we separate</i> ♪


01:30:43.663 --> 01:30:46.028
Don't go! Stop the car!


01:30:46.163 --> 01:30:48.701
-Tess?
-Don't go! Stop the engine!


01:30:48.837 --> 01:30:51.335
I'm not. The
engine's not even on.


01:30:51.471 --> 01:30:53.973
♪ <i>You hold it down When
I'm lost and found</i> ♪


01:30:54.109 --> 01:30:56.142
♪ <i>Look in my eyes
Be so profound</i> ♪


01:30:56.278 --> 01:30:58.144
♪ <i>Don't need to say a
thing We lose or win</i> ♪


01:30:58.279 --> 01:31:00.677
♪ <i>Together, you and
me We got everything</i> ♪


01:31:00.813 --> 01:31:03.520
♪ <i>One fine day</i> ♪


01:31:03.656 --> 01:31:05.951
♪ <i>Yeah We're going
there anyway</i> ♪


01:31:06.086 --> 01:31:09.092
-[Athena] Ella, he loves you!
-I love you!


01:31:09.228 --> 01:31:12.562
♪ <i>One fine day</i> ♪


01:31:13.925 --> 01:31:15.097
Cely, is everything okay?


01:31:15.233 --> 01:31:16.525
Yeah, everything's fine.


01:31:16.660 --> 01:31:17.703
Okay.


01:31:18.339 --> 01:31:19.995
I wonder what the
big emergency was.


01:31:20.130 --> 01:31:22.405
♪ <i>Happier happy days</i> ♪


01:31:22.541 --> 01:31:24.402
♪ <i>Right where I do belong</i> ♪


01:31:24.537 --> 01:31:25.542
Surprise!


01:31:26.145 --> 01:31:27.412
What are you doing here?


01:31:27.547 --> 01:31:28.897
Ella said you said
you missed performing.


01:31:28.980 --> 01:31:30.105
I...


01:31:30.241 --> 01:31:31.113
And that you told
her she could do


01:31:31.249 --> 01:31:32.249
any song she wanted to.


01:31:33.182 --> 01:31:34.476
You did?


01:31:34.612 --> 01:31:36.674
Dressing room is right around
the corner. Put this on.


01:31:36.757 --> 01:31:37.949
Why?


01:31:38.084 --> 01:31:39.370
Well, because we're
not 15 anymore.


01:31:39.453 --> 01:31:40.290
Dolphins.


01:31:40.425 --> 01:31:41.853
-Get in there. Okay.
-What?


01:31:41.989 --> 01:31:43.271
-Let me know when she's ready.
-Crazy.


01:31:43.354 --> 01:31:44.543
I can't believe you're
making me do this.


01:31:44.626 --> 01:31:45.955
Don't make fun of my dress.


